WEBVTT

00:15.015 --> 00:17.350
[theme music playing]

00:56.556 --> 01:00.977
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:06.900 --> 01:09.152
HYEREUNG KINDERGARTEN
BAE SEOK-RYU

01:09.944 --> 01:11.780
[quirky music playing]

01:14.365 --> 01:15.950
[young Seok-ryu] I lost a tooth today.

01:16.034 --> 01:17.035
[chuckles softly]

01:17.911 --> 01:20.789
My tooth is cute,
so I think the Tooth Fairy will like it.

01:21.539 --> 01:22.665
[Mi-suk] Open your mouth.

01:24.000 --> 01:24.959
There. It's tied.

01:26.127 --> 01:28.671
[Seung-hyo] I remember
all of Seok-ryu's firsts.

01:28.755 --> 01:30.173
-[exclaims]
-[young Seok-ryu yelps]

01:30.840 --> 01:31.674
Ow…

01:32.425 --> 01:34.302
-[Mi-suk] Look!
-[young Seok-ryu] Wow.

01:35.428 --> 01:37.430
Look at this. Isn't it cute?

01:37.514 --> 01:39.140
[crying]

01:40.767 --> 01:42.602
Why are you crying? It's not your tooth!

01:42.685 --> 01:44.813
-[continues crying]
-It's mine!

01:45.355 --> 01:46.272
Seung-hyo!

01:47.065 --> 01:49.192
[Seung-hyo] The first time
she lost a tooth.

01:49.275 --> 01:50.735
-[bell ringing]
-[boy 1 taunting]

01:50.819 --> 01:52.529
[boy 2] You can't even keep up, dummy!

01:52.612 --> 01:53.696
[boy 3] You're so slow!

01:53.780 --> 01:55.365
[boy 2] You dummy!

01:58.076 --> 01:59.911
How dare they call me a dummy?

02:00.912 --> 02:03.706
I'm going to blow by all of you!

02:03.790 --> 02:06.626
Hey!

02:09.587 --> 02:10.547
Hey, Seok-ryu!

02:10.630 --> 02:11.589
That's dangerous!

02:11.673 --> 02:13.174
[young Seok-ryu screaming]

02:15.927 --> 02:17.053
[indistinct chatter]

02:18.721 --> 02:20.348
[laughing]

02:20.431 --> 02:22.475
[Seung-hyo] The first time
she rode a bicycle.

02:22.559 --> 02:24.269
[bell ringing]

02:24.352 --> 02:25.895
[seagull squawks]

02:50.044 --> 02:53.715
I want to go back!

02:56.509 --> 02:59.387
Jeez, what is wrong with her?

03:02.348 --> 03:04.475
The first time she ran away from home.

03:04.559 --> 03:06.394
-[girls laughing]
-[Seok-ryu] Hey!

03:07.770 --> 03:09.314
This is how I feel about you.

03:10.106 --> 03:11.858
-Please take it.
-[boy] Don't.

03:11.941 --> 03:13.651
Look, I'm a senior.

03:14.736 --> 03:15.862
Don't give this to me.

03:15.945 --> 03:17.196
[mellow music playing]

03:17.280 --> 03:18.656
Don't have feelings for me.

03:19.532 --> 03:20.950
Okay?

03:21.534 --> 03:22.368
Sorry.

03:24.913 --> 03:26.873
[Seung-hyo] The first time
she asked someone out.

03:30.460 --> 03:33.338
-[boy] Hey, you're getting it everywhere!
-[girl] What's he doing?

03:41.429 --> 03:43.598
[Seung-hyo] I've known her for so long.

03:44.682 --> 03:46.768
I thought I knew everything about her.

03:49.103 --> 03:51.272
[breathes deeply]

03:52.649 --> 03:55.526
[young Seok-ryu] My dad
used to work as a chef at a hotel.

03:56.486 --> 03:58.404
Then, he worked at a restaurant.

03:58.488 --> 04:00.740
Now, he runs a tteokbokki shop.

04:00.823 --> 04:03.826
My dad's tteokbokki
is the best in the world!

04:03.910 --> 04:05.828
[Mi-suk] Seok-ryu!

04:05.912 --> 04:06.996
Hey, Seok-ryu!

04:07.080 --> 04:07.956
Coming!

04:12.585 --> 04:13.419
[door opens]

04:14.545 --> 04:15.380
[door closes]

04:18.883 --> 04:25.848
YOUR FIRST

04:26.724 --> 04:28.101
Seok-ryu!

04:29.269 --> 04:32.605
[Seok-ryu] You've been calling me
since the crack of dawn.

04:32.689 --> 04:34.941
What is all of this? It smells good.

04:35.024 --> 04:36.859
What else? They're side dishes.

04:36.943 --> 04:38.736
Take these to Seung-hyo's house.

04:38.820 --> 04:42.031
I don't want to. Did you make this
with the soy sauce I brought?

04:42.115 --> 04:45.827
Yeah, I think its quality
really brings out the savoriness.

04:50.623 --> 04:53.584
You're right! It's so good.

04:53.668 --> 04:54.919
What did you put in here?

04:55.003 --> 04:56.921
I made broth with anchovy stock,

04:57.005 --> 05:01.175
and I mixed it with chopped green onions,
garlic, sesame oil, and soy sauce…

05:01.259 --> 05:02.343
As if you'd know.

05:02.427 --> 05:03.803
I might know.

05:03.886 --> 05:04.971
Enough nonsense.

05:05.054 --> 05:06.639
Deliver these before they cool.

05:07.390 --> 05:08.766
Okay.

05:12.103 --> 05:13.104
Geun-sik!

05:14.314 --> 05:15.523
[door opens]

05:15.606 --> 05:17.775
-Come have breakfast.
-[door closes]

05:20.945 --> 05:21.988
[refrigerator door closes]

05:32.540 --> 05:33.833
I'm eating breakfast.

05:34.959 --> 05:35.877
Do you want some too?

05:35.960 --> 05:39.213
It's okay.
Rice is too heavy for breakfast.

05:43.426 --> 05:44.635
[doorbell rings]

05:48.765 --> 05:49.891
It's Seok-ryu.

05:49.974 --> 05:50.975
[door lock buzzes]

05:51.726 --> 05:53.436
-Seok-ryu!
-[Seok-ryu] Aunt Hye-suk!

05:53.519 --> 05:56.147
-It's been so long.
-[Hye-suk] Hi. I know!

05:56.230 --> 05:58.858
I haven't seen you
since Seung-hyo's opening.

05:58.941 --> 06:00.276
Let's meet often while I'm here.

06:00.359 --> 06:01.360
-What is this?
-Okay.

06:01.444 --> 06:03.488
-Mr. Choi!
-What brings you here this early?

06:03.571 --> 06:04.822
I'm here to deliver food.

06:04.906 --> 06:06.657
You happened to be eating too.

06:06.741 --> 06:08.701
Perfect timing! My mom said to give these.

06:08.785 --> 06:10.328
She did?

06:10.411 --> 06:14.499
Yeah, she made so much.
You know how she makes tons of food.

06:14.582 --> 06:16.209
She's always making food for us.

06:16.292 --> 06:17.877
Tell her we said thank you.

06:17.960 --> 06:19.128
Yes, sir!

06:19.212 --> 06:20.379
Is Choisseung upstairs?

06:20.463 --> 06:22.799
Yeah, of course.

06:22.882 --> 06:24.842
-I'll just say hi before I go!
-[Hye-suk] Okay.

06:24.926 --> 06:26.594
-[Seok-ryu] Enjoy your meal.
-Thanks.

06:26.677 --> 06:28.513
-Okay, go on!
-[Seok-ryu] All right!

06:28.596 --> 06:30.223
Why did she send so much?

06:31.224 --> 06:34.727
Goodness, stir-fried zucchini
with salted shrimp.

06:36.104 --> 06:38.606
Marinated perilla leaves
and pickled chili peppers.

06:38.689 --> 06:39.774
[quirky music playing]

06:40.775 --> 06:41.984
[refrigerator door closes]

06:42.068 --> 06:44.737
Wow! It's seasoned bracken!

06:45.738 --> 06:46.739
[Hye-suk sniffs, exhales]

06:47.657 --> 06:48.616
Bracken…

06:52.745 --> 06:55.456
You're making toast,
but these smell too strong, right?

06:55.540 --> 06:57.083
No, it's fine!

06:58.501 --> 06:59.335
Eat up.

07:03.840 --> 07:05.466
-[cutlery clinking]
-[gulps]

07:11.681 --> 07:14.600
Jeez, he's so clueless.

07:15.768 --> 07:18.062
Wow!

07:21.524 --> 07:22.608
[Seok-ryu] Hey, Choisseung!

07:27.697 --> 07:28.823
Is he in the bathroom?

07:30.324 --> 07:33.411
His room hasn't changed at all.

07:34.036 --> 07:35.830
Did I get in a time machine?

07:38.416 --> 07:39.542
The time capsule!

07:40.877 --> 07:44.422
I'm sure he hid it in here.

07:44.505 --> 07:46.257
[sucking air through teeth]

07:46.340 --> 07:48.301
Did you hide it here?

07:49.969 --> 07:51.679
I found it!

07:51.762 --> 07:54.765
This time, I'm going to
reveal your dark past.

08:11.824 --> 08:13.409
[pleasant music playing]

08:28.341 --> 08:30.676
[breathes deeply]

08:34.472 --> 08:36.807
YOU PROBABLY TOLD SEOK-RYU
HOW YOU FELT, RIGHT?

08:36.891 --> 08:39.101
WE'VE BEEN INSEPARABLE SINCE KIDS

08:54.408 --> 08:55.576
I'm sorry.

08:55.660 --> 08:58.079
I wasn't trying to secretly read it.

08:59.247 --> 09:02.166
I mean, you got to read my letter,
so it didn't feel fair.

09:02.875 --> 09:04.043
That's why I read it.

09:10.341 --> 09:12.843
-Why would you throw it away?
-Did you read it, right?

09:13.636 --> 09:16.222
-I did.
-It was a joke.

09:16.931 --> 09:18.307
A joke?

09:18.391 --> 09:20.476
I guess I was serious
about teasing you back then,

09:21.018 --> 09:22.353
seeing how far my pranks went.

09:22.436 --> 09:23.729
[chuckles softly]

09:23.813 --> 09:26.148
Yeah! It's just a joke, right?

09:27.608 --> 09:29.527
Hey, you startled me!

09:31.904 --> 09:33.906
I thought it'd be funny, but it's not.

09:34.448 --> 09:35.616
[chuckles softly]

09:35.700 --> 09:37.159
I have to change. Can you get out?

09:37.243 --> 09:39.579
Yeah, sure! Sorry. Get dressed.

09:43.374 --> 09:44.250
[phone vibrating]

09:44.333 --> 09:46.168
JANG TAE-HUI

09:51.299 --> 09:53.175
What was with that letter?

09:54.385 --> 09:57.722
Did he like me? But it was a joke?

09:57.805 --> 10:01.559
Why would he plan a joke for 10 years?
What are they, economic reforms?

10:02.643 --> 10:04.562
He could've just said it wasn't true.

10:04.645 --> 10:06.897
Why did he crumple it up and toss it?

10:10.943 --> 10:13.446
What? Dad hasn't come in yet.

10:15.197 --> 10:17.491
ROOT DINER

10:17.575 --> 10:19.910
[door lock beeps]

10:27.209 --> 10:28.044
[sighs]

10:30.212 --> 10:32.340
This place hasn't changed either.

10:35.926 --> 10:39.555
[Geun-sik] Wow, my girl's so good!

10:40.389 --> 10:42.266
I wonder who you take after
to be this good.

10:42.350 --> 10:44.935
-You.
-Me? [chuckles]

10:46.145 --> 10:50.191
Should I taste your food
and see how good it is?

10:50.274 --> 10:51.317
Okay?

10:52.026 --> 10:53.527
Let's see…

10:54.695 --> 10:55.655
Is it good?

10:57.698 --> 10:58.991
My goodness.

10:59.075 --> 11:00.785
What? Is it bad?

11:01.786 --> 11:02.787
It's so good!

11:02.870 --> 11:06.499
It's so good!
My precious girl, it's so good!

11:06.582 --> 11:08.668
[both chuckling]

11:10.753 --> 11:12.838
-Goodness, I'm so proud of you.
-[giggles]

11:17.176 --> 11:18.803
-[exhales]
-[doorbell chiming]

11:19.845 --> 11:21.889
Hey. Seok-ryu!

11:21.972 --> 11:22.973
[Seok-ryu] Dad.

11:23.599 --> 11:26.227
What are you doing here?
Did you pick the lock to get in?

11:26.310 --> 11:27.269
I entered the key code.

11:27.353 --> 11:28.354
Was no one else here?

11:28.437 --> 11:30.106
Why are you so flustered?

11:30.189 --> 11:32.191
Are you worried there might be a thief?

11:32.274 --> 11:34.443
There's nothing to steal here.

11:34.527 --> 11:37.613
No, I was just worried
because the door was open.

11:38.406 --> 11:40.950
Why would you come here
without telling me?

11:41.784 --> 11:43.160
Dad, do you remember?

11:43.244 --> 11:44.995
I used to hang around here a lot as a kid.

11:45.079 --> 11:47.456
-[water running]
-You practically lived here.

11:48.249 --> 11:52.211
You'd always follow me
into the kitchen and mess around.

11:52.294 --> 11:54.755
[Seok-ryu chuckles] You're right.

11:54.839 --> 12:00.052
In the past, you used to work at a hotel
and even worked at a big restaurant.

12:00.719 --> 12:02.930
But I loved it the most
when you worked here.

12:04.223 --> 12:05.683
When you worked at the hotel,

12:05.766 --> 12:08.352
you wore that tall hat
and I only saw you in photos.

12:08.436 --> 12:10.062
I never actually saw you work.

12:10.688 --> 12:12.022
And the restaurant was too busy.

12:12.106 --> 12:15.192
But I loved
that I could come here all the time.

12:15.276 --> 12:16.235
[chuckles softly]

12:17.445 --> 12:20.197
It's strange,
but I still remember how I felt back then.

12:21.532 --> 12:23.117
The sound of the knife cutting.

12:24.118 --> 12:25.995
The low and steady warmth of the air.

12:27.329 --> 12:28.789
The sound of people.

12:29.331 --> 12:30.541
Seeing you work from the back.

12:31.917 --> 12:34.044
And the tastiest tteokbokki
in the world.

12:37.256 --> 12:38.382
That's good to hear.

12:39.717 --> 12:41.427
-[Seok-ryu] Dad?
-Yeah?

12:41.510 --> 12:42.595
What if…

12:43.596 --> 12:46.015
What if I became a cook like you?

12:46.098 --> 12:47.892
What are you saying?

12:47.975 --> 12:49.351
It's a relief you didn't!

12:50.936 --> 12:51.770
Why?

12:51.854 --> 12:52.938
I made you study hard

12:53.022 --> 12:56.275
so you wouldn't have to get your hands wet
or stand in front of a hot stove.

12:56.358 --> 12:58.277
Leave this kind of work to me.

12:58.360 --> 12:59.445
[chuckles]

13:01.155 --> 13:02.656
-[Geun-sik] Seok-ryu.
-Yeah?

13:02.740 --> 13:04.450
Want some tteokbokki before you go?

13:04.533 --> 13:05.910
Sounds good.

13:05.993 --> 13:07.119
Okay. [chuckles]

13:07.203 --> 13:08.412
Wait right there.

13:10.664 --> 13:13.083
[objects clattering]

13:13.167 --> 13:15.127
THE CHUNGWOO DAILY

13:15.211 --> 13:16.504
[exhales]

13:16.587 --> 13:17.922
Wait a second!

13:19.632 --> 13:21.717
Goodness. Thank you. [panting]

13:25.137 --> 13:27.598
I would've pressed "Close"
if I knew it was you.

13:27.681 --> 13:30.726
That would've hurt
your performance review. [chuckles softly]

13:32.311 --> 13:33.687
How's Yeon-du? Is she okay?

13:33.771 --> 13:37.691
Yes, she was discharged.
She went to kindergarten this morning.

13:37.775 --> 13:39.235
What a relief.

13:40.486 --> 13:43.739
Kids always get sick
when the seasons change.

13:43.822 --> 13:45.449
It's to worry their parents.

13:45.533 --> 13:47.493
Could you transfer me
to a different department?

13:48.035 --> 13:50.496
-What?
-I know you did a lot to accommodate me.

13:51.539 --> 13:53.832
But the social affairs team
will be fine even without me.

13:54.833 --> 13:57.920
My daughter needs me the most right now.

13:59.547 --> 14:01.966
I had three kids as I stayed on this job.

14:02.049 --> 14:05.052
I know. That's why I respect you.

14:05.135 --> 14:06.887
I'm not trying to brag.

14:08.055 --> 14:11.600
I probably would've left
if my husband weren't a freelancer.

14:12.601 --> 14:14.770
It must be hard raising her on your own.

14:14.853 --> 14:16.105
[elevator rings]

14:17.314 --> 14:18.566
But kids grow up fast.

14:22.695 --> 14:24.071
Give it another thought.

14:24.154 --> 14:27.533
And if you still want to leave then,
I won't try to stop you.

14:35.082 --> 14:35.916
[exhales]

14:48.137 --> 14:49.680
[pleasant music playing]

14:55.311 --> 14:57.104
[Seok-ryu over tablet]
You know how in the US

14:57.187 --> 15:00.190
we have chicken soup
when we're not feeling so well?

15:00.858 --> 15:05.154
I guess it's because it's so comforting,
and it warms you up from the inside.

15:05.988 --> 15:08.574
Well, Korea has its own chicken soup,

15:08.657 --> 15:10.534
which we will be making today.

15:10.618 --> 15:11.493
The samgyejuk.

15:11.577 --> 15:14.955
The ingredients are as you see here.

15:17.541 --> 15:21.837
So let me start by preparing the chicken.

15:23.631 --> 15:26.926
I had an important presentation
earlier today,

15:27.009 --> 15:30.596
so you can imagine
what a tense day it has been for me.

15:31.513 --> 15:35.684
That's why I wanted
to comfort my tired soul,

15:35.768 --> 15:38.479
not just with food but by cooking.

15:40.064 --> 15:45.569
Because personally for me,
it's a very soothing ritual.

15:46.362 --> 15:47.488
As I cook,

15:47.571 --> 15:50.866
I get very comfortable and I just unwind.

15:50.950 --> 15:55.412
I feel like totally myself
when I'm at ease.

16:28.737 --> 16:30.906
[Tae-hui] Hey, Seok-ryu.
It's been a while!

16:30.990 --> 16:31.865
Hello!

16:34.952 --> 16:37.121
-Why aren't you saying hi?
-Why? I see her every day.

16:39.415 --> 16:41.375
-You took your cast off.
-Yeah.

16:46.255 --> 16:49.675
Thank you so much
for the soy sauce the other day.

16:49.758 --> 16:52.511
It tastes absolutely amazing.
My family loves it.

16:52.594 --> 16:54.596
Let me know if you need more.

16:54.680 --> 16:56.932
Do you have time to come in for tea?

16:57.016 --> 16:58.392
Tea?

16:59.601 --> 17:01.895
We have work to talk about.
Why are you inviting her?

17:02.396 --> 17:03.689
We need to go over Fresco.

17:03.772 --> 17:05.733
We need to decide
on the direction and schedule.

17:06.275 --> 17:08.235
Yeah, okay.

17:09.361 --> 17:11.864
I was busy anyway.

17:11.947 --> 17:14.033
I'm sure you're busy. You should go.

17:14.116 --> 17:16.660
I'm sorry, Seok-ryu. Let's meet up later.

17:23.667 --> 17:24.626
[scoffs]

17:24.710 --> 17:27.046
He went nuts when I said
to work things out with her.

17:27.713 --> 17:29.298
Now, I'm an unwelcome guest?

17:30.758 --> 17:32.217
Like me? Yeah, right.

17:32.301 --> 17:34.762
Forget it.
I don't care about that letter either.

17:42.394 --> 17:43.479
What's the reason?

17:44.813 --> 17:47.816
I see you still ask random questions
without any context.

17:47.900 --> 17:48.859
I don't understand.

17:50.027 --> 17:51.987
Tell me why you agreed to work with me.

17:52.071 --> 17:55.115
It seemed like a good opportunity.
I thought it'd be fun to try.

17:56.658 --> 17:57.910
How predictable.

17:58.577 --> 17:59.578
What did you expect?

17:59.661 --> 18:01.246
POMEGRANATE TREE

18:01.330 --> 18:04.917
I don't know. Something more honest.

18:06.585 --> 18:08.504
I know you used me as an excuse today.

18:10.547 --> 18:12.132
You were silent the whole time,

18:12.216 --> 18:15.219
but in front of Seok-ryu,
you said on purpose we had to work.

18:15.928 --> 18:17.221
Sorry if it seemed that way.

18:20.933 --> 18:23.769
Since it's turned out this way,
how about just using me?

18:24.853 --> 18:28.107
-What?
-Use me the best you can.

18:28.774 --> 18:31.777
It'll be nice.
I'd get to go on dates with you,

18:31.860 --> 18:33.529
and you can face your feelings.

18:34.822 --> 18:36.615
Do you want to be thrown out?

18:36.698 --> 18:38.158
Come on.

18:38.242 --> 18:39.618
I think Seok-ryu's cute.

18:39.701 --> 18:42.162
Of course, you're cuter.

18:43.163 --> 18:45.415
Can't I hang out
with you two cuties a bit longer?

18:45.499 --> 18:48.085
You can tease me all you want,

18:48.168 --> 18:49.586
but don't say anything to Seok-ryu.

18:52.172 --> 18:53.173
[sighs audibly]

18:53.841 --> 18:56.510
I think you already told her
something important.

18:57.219 --> 18:58.220
What?

18:59.721 --> 19:01.849
But there's something you left out.

19:02.474 --> 19:04.518
I should ask her to grab a bite later.

19:04.601 --> 19:06.103
What did I tell her?

19:06.186 --> 19:07.980
I mean, what are you going to say?

19:08.981 --> 19:09.857
I'm not telling you.

19:09.940 --> 19:10.774
What did I say?

19:10.858 --> 19:12.943
-If I tell you, you'll let me join in?
-Tae-hui!

19:13.026 --> 19:15.529
I love it when you call my name.

19:15.612 --> 19:17.531
What did I say?

19:17.614 --> 19:19.283
What are you going to tell her?

19:19.366 --> 19:20.742
[upbeat music playing]

19:25.414 --> 19:27.457
[instructor] Accelerate
and maintain cruising speed.

19:27.541 --> 19:29.001
Proceeding to cruising speed.

19:29.084 --> 19:31.253
[engine accelerating]

19:31.962 --> 19:33.172
[Seok-ryu exhales]

19:33.255 --> 19:36.175
I wondered
what you were doing at the river.

19:36.258 --> 19:38.635
-Who knew you'd be on a boat?
-[exhales]

19:38.719 --> 19:42.890
I passed the written test, so I need
to practice for the in-person exam.

19:42.973 --> 19:45.350
You're about to overtake
the land, air, and sea.

19:45.434 --> 19:48.020
What's next?
A light aircraft pilot license?

19:48.103 --> 19:48.937
Next is…

19:49.771 --> 19:51.148
-The South Pole.
-What?

19:52.065 --> 19:55.277
There's a paramedic who was sent
to the research station there.

19:56.195 --> 19:58.572
This license will earn
extra points for it.

19:58.655 --> 20:00.908
Wow, that's so like you.

20:00.991 --> 20:05.662
You'd walk in puddles,
mud, and wet cement as a kid,

20:05.746 --> 20:08.165
always picking paths
others wouldn't travel.

20:08.248 --> 20:10.709
You're finally venturing
into uncharted territory.

20:10.792 --> 20:11.877
[Mo-eum] Come on.

20:11.960 --> 20:14.755
Hey. Don't count your chickens
before they hatch.

20:14.838 --> 20:15.756
[clears throat]

20:16.590 --> 20:19.468
Documents, interviews,
and personality and aptitude tests.

20:20.135 --> 20:21.720
I have a long way to go to be selected.

20:21.803 --> 20:24.556
I'm the one with a long way to go.

20:24.640 --> 20:25.807
What?

20:26.642 --> 20:28.185
I registered for a cooking class.

20:29.519 --> 20:30.479
Holy cow.

20:30.562 --> 20:32.606
I thought long and hard about it.

20:34.316 --> 20:35.651
I think I want to do it.

20:38.487 --> 20:40.072
No, I want to do it.

20:40.155 --> 20:45.619
In the past, I thought studying
was your favorite thing to do.

20:45.702 --> 20:47.704
But I was wrong.

20:47.788 --> 20:52.542
You just liked the praise and attention
that came from studying well.

20:53.252 --> 20:54.795
You went crazy for the extra stuff.

20:54.878 --> 20:56.964
You've been brutally honest a lot lately.

20:57.047 --> 20:58.715
Yes, but…

20:58.799 --> 21:00.550
You loved to cook.

21:01.051 --> 21:03.762
It was a pure and selfless love.

21:05.931 --> 21:10.227
I should've known you were destined for it
when I saw you make perfect dalgonas.

21:11.979 --> 21:14.314
-Are you cheering me on?
-Of course.

21:14.398 --> 21:15.691
[clears throat]

21:15.774 --> 21:18.777
Let's celebrate today.

21:18.860 --> 21:21.780
Let's call Seung-hyo over
and have a party.

21:21.863 --> 21:23.031
Hey.

21:23.115 --> 21:23.949
Hello?

21:24.658 --> 21:25.617
Seung-hyo!

21:25.701 --> 21:27.077
-Hey, don't.
-[Mo-eum] Wait.

21:28.120 --> 21:31.206
Seok-ryu said she registered
for cooking classes today.

21:32.374 --> 21:34.126
She registered for cooking classes?

21:35.043 --> 21:36.586
Yeah…

21:36.670 --> 21:41.049
Well, on that note,
let's have a party to celebrate tonight.

21:41.925 --> 21:43.677
I can't go. I have plans.

21:44.261 --> 21:46.596
Really? Okay.

21:46.680 --> 21:49.808
Then, come after you're done.
I'll text you the location later.

21:50.475 --> 21:51.560
Bye.

21:53.979 --> 21:54.896
[call disconnects]

21:58.317 --> 21:59.234
[sighs softly]

22:00.319 --> 22:02.195
Why say that if he can't make it?

22:02.279 --> 22:03.905
Don't you know him at all?

22:04.698 --> 22:07.159
He always says he can't come but he does.

22:07.242 --> 22:08.827
He really won't come today.

22:09.494 --> 22:10.454
What's this?

22:12.331 --> 22:13.415
Did you two fight again?

22:21.381 --> 22:22.883
[Dan-ho] Mr. Choi?

22:23.550 --> 22:24.384
Oh.

22:25.135 --> 22:27.596
It's nice to run into you
around the town like this.

22:27.679 --> 22:29.556
I feel the same. Are you going home?

22:29.639 --> 22:32.934
No, I'm thinking of getting a drink.
Do you want to join me?

22:33.518 --> 22:34.352
Oh.

22:36.396 --> 22:37.856
[inhales] Well…

22:41.610 --> 22:42.736
This is it.

22:46.865 --> 22:47.699
[Seung-hyo] Oh.

22:47.783 --> 22:50.202
You live next door to Jung Mo-eum?

22:50.285 --> 22:53.288
Yes, I just learned that recently.

22:53.371 --> 22:54.664
I see. [chuckles softly]

22:56.208 --> 22:58.543
Try to be understanding
if things get loud.

22:58.627 --> 22:59.878
She's a good person.

22:59.961 --> 23:00.962
I know.

23:02.589 --> 23:05.425
But I feel bad about making you come here.

23:05.509 --> 23:06.927
It was due to circumstances.

23:07.010 --> 23:08.136
Daddy!

23:08.845 --> 23:09.721
[Dan-ho] Yeon-du.

23:09.805 --> 23:10.806
[door closes]

23:10.889 --> 23:13.642
My girl, did you wait a long for me?

23:13.725 --> 23:14.726
[Yeon-du] Yeah.

23:16.686 --> 23:18.271
This is my daughter.

23:18.355 --> 23:20.023
Yeon-du, say hi.

23:20.107 --> 23:22.943
Hello, I'm Kang Yeon-du.

23:23.026 --> 23:24.361
But who are you?

23:27.197 --> 23:29.199
I'm Choi Seung-hyo.

23:29.783 --> 23:30.784
I am…

23:32.577 --> 23:33.829
your dad's…

23:34.579 --> 23:35.580
neighborhood friend.

23:37.999 --> 23:39.167
[chuckles softly]

23:39.251 --> 23:40.460
[pleasant music playing]

23:42.879 --> 23:43.713
[exclaims]

23:44.548 --> 23:45.674
[Dan-ho] I'm sorry.

23:46.508 --> 23:49.845
I'm sure misugaru wasn't the drink
you were talking about.

23:51.096 --> 23:53.807
No, this is exactly what I wanted.

23:53.890 --> 23:55.016
With a lot of ice too.

23:55.100 --> 23:56.309
[Dan-ho chuckles]

23:59.521 --> 24:00.522
[exhales]

24:01.523 --> 24:05.235
I haven't had any alcohol,
but I oddly feel like I'm getting drunk.

24:06.695 --> 24:08.363
I guess this neighborhood does that?

24:08.989 --> 24:12.200
It's my first time here,
but I feel like I've lived here forever.

24:12.909 --> 24:14.494
It's strangely relaxing.

24:16.037 --> 24:17.289
And it makes me excited.

24:20.208 --> 24:23.461
I've experienced that too,
and this place is like that.

24:24.462 --> 24:25.589
You're adjusting well.

24:26.756 --> 24:29.176
Yes, thanks to my neighborhood friend.

24:35.682 --> 24:38.143
Can I ask you why
you wanted to drink tonight?

24:39.227 --> 24:40.729
-Sorry?
-Well…

24:41.813 --> 24:44.274
I guess it's a habit from work.

24:44.357 --> 24:47.068
I read people's faces.

24:47.152 --> 24:49.362
I ask incessantly
if I'm curious about something.

24:50.447 --> 24:52.908
Maybe that's why people hate reporters.

24:53.700 --> 24:55.869
Well, it looks like you already knew.

24:55.952 --> 24:56.870
[Dan-ho chuckles]

24:57.662 --> 24:58.872
Of course.

24:59.789 --> 25:02.334
However, I'm good with the opposite too.

25:03.043 --> 25:07.422
I'm a good listener. I can be neutral.
And I can guarantee anonymity.

25:09.883 --> 25:11.968
I just thought I could be of some help.

25:19.893 --> 25:21.394
It's about my friend, not me.

25:23.772 --> 25:26.358
There's someone he liked a long time ago.

25:29.236 --> 25:31.905
He thought he'd moved on
from his feelings for her.

25:33.073 --> 25:35.575
But he's a bit confused
after seeing her again.

25:37.452 --> 25:38.578
That's understandable.

25:40.455 --> 25:43.875
He doesn't know what to do,
so he keeps avoiding her.

25:43.959 --> 25:46.127
-I think he's having a hard time.
-[Dan-ho] Mmm.

25:47.045 --> 25:49.005
Is it something that can't happen?

25:49.089 --> 25:51.299
For example, is she seeing someone else?

25:53.385 --> 25:56.680
She's in love with someone else.
They almost got married.

25:58.181 --> 26:00.558
In any case, she's single now, right?

26:01.643 --> 26:03.979
As for this woman,

26:04.062 --> 26:05.897
does she know how your friend feels?

26:06.940 --> 26:07.941
No.

26:09.150 --> 26:11.569
But he's scared she might find out.

26:13.822 --> 26:16.616
He's never confessed
his feelings to her before.

26:17.534 --> 26:18.618
Why not?

26:19.452 --> 26:20.996
They've always been together,

26:21.788 --> 26:24.499
so he didn't know the true nature
of those feelings at first.

26:25.083 --> 26:26.251
After that…

26:28.461 --> 26:30.463
he was cautious
to not ruin their friendship.

26:31.715 --> 26:33.133
When he did decide to tell her…

26:34.426 --> 26:35.802
the timing was off.

26:38.221 --> 26:39.306
And now…

26:44.311 --> 26:45.645
he can't even dare to try.

26:48.148 --> 26:50.442
He had a hard time
for a while because of that.

26:51.234 --> 26:54.029
He'd get nauseous and dizzy.

26:56.823 --> 26:58.658
He's finally settled down now

27:01.953 --> 27:04.080
and doesn't want to go back to that time.

27:06.124 --> 27:07.709
[quirky music playing]

27:10.378 --> 27:12.589
No wonder he didn't come today.

27:14.632 --> 27:15.717
[Mo-eum exclaims]

27:22.891 --> 27:26.061
I'm so curious. How can I wait 10 years?

27:29.564 --> 27:32.233
All right. Let's see here.

27:35.570 --> 27:37.113
Whose letter is this?

27:37.197 --> 27:39.366
It must be Seung-hyo's.

27:43.578 --> 27:44.412
[exclaims]

27:46.956 --> 27:49.709
[laughing] I knew it!

27:50.710 --> 27:52.670
Just tell her that you like her.

27:52.754 --> 27:54.631
Why does he make it so hard on himself?

27:55.256 --> 27:57.008
I swear…

27:58.385 --> 27:59.928
Jeez, he's so pathetic.

28:00.887 --> 28:02.847
He's still as dumb as ever.

28:04.265 --> 28:05.266
[scoffs]

28:06.518 --> 28:08.812
Did you hear that strange noise?

28:10.522 --> 28:11.523
Not really.

28:12.148 --> 28:13.024
I don't know.

28:14.526 --> 28:15.652
Was I mistaken?

28:17.070 --> 28:19.697
Then, is your friend going to continue

28:19.781 --> 28:22.325
to pretend like he doesn't like her

28:23.076 --> 28:24.411
and push her away?

28:26.079 --> 28:27.956
He says he's trying for now.

28:28.665 --> 28:30.625
If he were my friend,

28:31.418 --> 28:33.878
I'd tell him about a swimmer I know.

28:34.879 --> 28:37.757
There once was an athlete
in the 200-meter event

28:37.841 --> 28:40.969
whose weakness was
being slow off the blocks.

28:41.052 --> 28:44.013
But despite this, he overcame it
through his tireless efforts.

28:44.597 --> 28:46.099
[mellow music playing]

28:46.891 --> 28:48.101
Even if it's a bit late,

28:48.643 --> 28:52.230
I'd tell him to muster up the courage,
just like the swimmer did.

28:54.399 --> 28:55.316
[exhales]

28:59.988 --> 29:00.905
[sighs softly]

29:06.161 --> 29:07.328
[Mi-suk] Get up!

29:07.412 --> 29:08.496
I said get up!

29:09.122 --> 29:11.458
[Geun-sik] I'm up.

29:12.417 --> 29:15.545
You should wake up early in the morning
and get ready for work.

29:15.628 --> 29:17.213
We're not even ready to retire.

29:17.297 --> 29:19.340
What have you accomplished
to afford to be lazy?

29:19.424 --> 29:21.259
Okay, stop it.

29:21.342 --> 29:22.802
Stop what?

29:22.886 --> 29:26.639
Thinking about all the money we've lost
is enough to keep me up at night.

29:26.723 --> 29:29.434
Why are you bringing up
things from the past again?

29:29.517 --> 29:31.644
The past? Things are still the same now.

29:31.728 --> 29:35.899
And when did you come home last night?
I woke up to you sleeping next to me.

29:35.982 --> 29:38.151
I told you. I went to a funeral.

29:38.234 --> 29:41.154
Gosh, you went to a funeral
the other night and the night before.

29:41.237 --> 29:43.573
You're just going around giving money.

29:43.656 --> 29:46.451
This is why I hate coming home.

29:46.534 --> 29:49.204
What? You have no right to be shouting!

29:49.287 --> 29:50.288
Whatever.

29:50.914 --> 29:53.291
Look! You're running away
because you have nothing to say!

29:53.374 --> 29:56.628
-I'm not done yet! Come home early.
-[Geun-sik] I have a class reunion today!

29:56.711 --> 29:57.670
[Mi-suk] Again?

29:57.754 --> 29:59.047
Are you kidding me?

29:59.130 --> 30:00.048
[phone vibrating]

30:01.466 --> 30:02.842
Unbelievable…

30:06.846 --> 30:08.681
Why are there insufficient funds?

30:09.265 --> 30:10.099
[gasps]

30:10.600 --> 30:12.602
Is this a new voice phishing scam?

30:23.446 --> 30:28.034
Hey, I'm saying this in advance to avoid
any misunderstanding. I'm just passing by.

30:28.117 --> 30:30.453
My cooking class is near here.

30:30.537 --> 30:31.788
I didn't say anything.

30:32.705 --> 30:35.291
I'm trying to get
my Korean Food Craftsman certificate.

30:37.418 --> 30:38.878
Don't tell my parents yet.

30:38.962 --> 30:40.630
I won't.

30:42.423 --> 30:44.217
Today's my first class.

30:44.300 --> 30:48.388
I looked over the curriculum,
and there's a written and in-person exam.

30:48.471 --> 30:51.474
And once class is over,
I get to take home whatever I make--

30:51.558 --> 30:53.059
I have a meeting.

30:53.601 --> 30:54.435
I'm off.

31:00.233 --> 31:01.234
What was that?

31:02.277 --> 31:04.612
He's the one who insisted
that I find my dream.

31:07.699 --> 31:10.660
KOREAN FOOD CRAFTSMAN

31:15.206 --> 31:17.125
WHAT DO KOREAN FOOD CRAFTSMAN DO?

31:21.796 --> 31:23.506
-[Myeong-u] The deodeok looks good.
-Jeez!

31:23.590 --> 31:25.258
Why did you suddenly close the window?

31:25.341 --> 31:27.051
What are you doing there?

31:27.135 --> 31:28.136
What are you doing?

31:28.219 --> 31:29.220
What?

31:30.513 --> 31:34.392
-Look at the time. Let's have the meeting.
-Isn't that for a certificate?

31:34.475 --> 31:35.643
Why are you looking at that?

31:36.394 --> 31:39.606
Na-yun, tell Hyeong-chan and Jeong-min
to come to the meeting room.

31:39.689 --> 31:41.316
Are you learning to cook? Korean food?

31:41.399 --> 31:42.942
I like Western cuisine.

31:43.026 --> 31:44.777
HYEREUNG COOKING SCHOOL

31:49.324 --> 31:52.702
[cooking teacher] Welcome
to the Korean Food Craftsman class.

31:52.785 --> 31:53.620
Hello.

31:53.703 --> 31:55.371
[all] Hello.

31:55.455 --> 31:56.414
[playful music playing]

31:56.497 --> 31:59.292
Today's our first class together.

31:59.375 --> 32:03.254
The first one's always memorable
and exciting.

32:03.338 --> 32:05.298
With that in mind, I'll make sure

32:05.381 --> 32:08.843
to give you a very raw
and memorable first experience.

32:09.802 --> 32:12.305
We'll be learning the basics
of knife skills today.

32:12.388 --> 32:14.223
You'll first learn basic techniques.

32:14.307 --> 32:17.352
Then, you'll start cutting radishes,
carrots, and other vegetables.

32:17.435 --> 32:20.772
All right, let's pick up
the knife that's in front of you.

32:21.814 --> 32:22.649
Okay, good.

32:23.524 --> 32:26.027
First, place the non-slip pad
on the counter

32:26.110 --> 32:27.779
and put the cutting board on top of it.

32:28.863 --> 32:32.867
Good. When putting knives down, make sure
the blade always faces away from you

32:32.951 --> 32:34.494
to not accidentally cut yourself.

32:34.577 --> 32:35.620
That's good.

32:36.245 --> 32:38.539
We're going to julienne the radish.

32:38.623 --> 32:42.001
First, peel the radish.

32:42.085 --> 32:47.173
Okay. Then, cut them into slices
about 0.2 centimeters thick.

32:56.057 --> 33:00.812
When preparing an omelet,
remove the chalazae from the yolk.

33:00.895 --> 33:03.940
Then, strain the egg whites
through a sieve.

33:04.023 --> 33:06.234
Whisk it smooth to avoid creating bubbles.

33:06.901 --> 33:11.155
Next, coat the pan with a thin layer
of oil over low heat.

33:22.250 --> 33:23.126
[indistinct chatter]

33:27.630 --> 33:29.007
[indistinct chatter]

33:30.675 --> 33:32.301
[lead worker] Hey, Mr. Choi!

33:32.385 --> 33:34.554
-Over here!
-Come sit down!

33:35.221 --> 33:37.974
Have you all been well?

33:38.057 --> 33:39.684
Not at all.

33:39.767 --> 33:41.936
Work sites have been a mess these days.

33:42.020 --> 33:44.063
It was great when we worked with you.

33:44.147 --> 33:46.441
What do you mean?
You hated me for being strict.

33:46.524 --> 33:48.109
I'd rather have someone strict.

33:48.192 --> 33:51.654
These people can't do their jobs
and always abuse their power,

33:51.738 --> 33:53.614
so it's been miserable working for them.

33:53.698 --> 33:57.618
Come on. You're not the type
to let a client walk all over you.

33:57.702 --> 33:59.829
Hold on. Are you mocking me?

33:59.912 --> 34:00.788
[all laughing]

34:00.872 --> 34:01.873
Well, prepare yourself.

34:01.956 --> 34:05.668
I'm going to punish you
with alcohol tonight!

34:05.752 --> 34:06.753
[all exclaiming]

34:08.337 --> 34:10.089
I drove tonight. I can't.

34:10.173 --> 34:12.008
Call a designated driver.

34:12.091 --> 34:14.302
Ma'am, can we get some soda
and another glass?

34:14.385 --> 34:15.219
[female staff] Okay!

34:15.303 --> 34:17.263
In return, dinner's on me tonight.

34:17.346 --> 34:18.890
[lead worker] What? Really?

34:18.973 --> 34:20.058
[all exclaiming]

34:21.517 --> 34:22.477
Okay!

34:22.560 --> 34:25.396
Then, instead of alcohol,

34:25.480 --> 34:28.775
-I'll punish you with meat instead!
-[workers laughing]

34:28.858 --> 34:30.109
-Open up!
-[Seung-hyo] Gosh.

34:32.904 --> 34:34.614
-Wow!
-[lead worker] Isn't it good?

34:34.697 --> 34:36.074
What is this? Why is it so good?

34:36.157 --> 34:37.742
I'm quite the gourmet.

34:37.825 --> 34:40.161
The taste of the meat here
is different from other places.

34:40.244 --> 34:43.247
-It's so juicy!
-[all laughing]

34:43.331 --> 34:45.625
You know our chief's philosophy.

34:45.708 --> 34:48.669
"Grease the wheels with delicious meat

34:48.753 --> 34:50.922
to keep the job running smoothly."

34:51.005 --> 34:52.965
-[workers] Huzzah!
-All right!

34:54.634 --> 34:56.302
[all chuckling]

34:56.385 --> 34:57.553
It's so good.

34:58.513 --> 35:00.181
[all exclaiming]

35:02.391 --> 35:04.102
I don't think this will be enough.

35:04.936 --> 35:07.814
Excuse me, could we have
more pork belly and short rib, please?

35:07.897 --> 35:09.107
And more beef brisket too!

35:09.190 --> 35:11.192
[all exclaiming, cheering]

35:12.026 --> 35:13.486
Gosh, what's this?

35:13.569 --> 35:15.488
What's this? Take it.

35:15.571 --> 35:16.656
Thank you very much.

35:16.739 --> 35:18.116
-[worker] Eat up.
-Thank you.

35:18.199 --> 35:20.701
I can't believe
you didn't have a single drink.

35:20.785 --> 35:22.203
You're so dogged!

35:22.286 --> 35:24.247
I'm sorry. I still have work left to do.

35:24.330 --> 35:26.916
You're drunk.
Don't go for another round of drinks.

35:26.999 --> 35:28.459
Make sure you go home, okay?

35:28.543 --> 35:30.294
Gosh, stop your nagging!

35:30.378 --> 35:33.422
Leave your car at home next time
and come on foot.

35:33.506 --> 35:35.007
Like this.

35:35.091 --> 35:37.343
-Yes, sir.
-[lead worker] Okay, see you next time.

35:37.426 --> 35:40.346
-Goodness.
-Chief! This way!

35:40.429 --> 35:42.557
I looked just like you when I was young!

35:44.308 --> 35:46.269
-See you later! Bye!
-Bye!

35:46.352 --> 35:47.353
Thank you for the meal.

35:47.436 --> 35:48.855
-Sure. Good night.
-Bye.

35:51.274 --> 35:52.525
[indistinct chatter]

35:56.112 --> 35:57.738
[lady exclaiming]

35:57.822 --> 35:59.824
-Sweetie, you're so cute!
-Yes?

36:00.491 --> 36:01.325
[lady] Over there.

36:02.118 --> 36:03.870
Do you want to come over?

36:04.370 --> 36:05.872
[Geun-sik] Where do you live?

36:05.955 --> 36:07.748
[indistinct conversation]

36:19.635 --> 36:22.054
[young Seung-hyo crying] Mom, don't go!

36:22.138 --> 36:23.890
[emotional music playing]

36:30.605 --> 36:31.814
[continues crying]

36:41.616 --> 36:43.326
[horn honking]

36:51.792 --> 36:53.544
[sighs deeply]

36:56.047 --> 36:58.049
[singing a song]

37:05.306 --> 37:06.432
[exclaims in surprise]

37:07.391 --> 37:08.517
Seung-hyo?

37:10.186 --> 37:12.480
What are you doing here?

37:16.442 --> 37:17.276
Hey.

37:21.656 --> 37:24.200
-Thanks for the drink.
-[Seung-hyo] It's nothing.

37:24.283 --> 37:25.952
I'm sorry I surprised you.

37:26.494 --> 37:29.538
Yeah, you startled me to death.

37:29.622 --> 37:33.209
Why were you sitting
outside our house at this hour?

37:34.293 --> 37:36.337
I didn't know what to do,
so I was thinking.

37:36.420 --> 37:37.421
What?

37:38.089 --> 37:40.633
To be honest, I saw you.

37:41.676 --> 37:42.927
You were with some woman.

37:46.514 --> 37:48.516
[mellow music playing]

37:58.401 --> 38:00.152
Is that what you've decided to do?

38:01.696 --> 38:03.864
Yeah, it is.

38:04.991 --> 38:06.742
It'll put me at ease.

38:11.247 --> 38:12.623
Goodness…

38:12.707 --> 38:15.626
I'm ashamed you had to see me like this.

38:18.921 --> 38:21.716
I know it's shameless to ask…

38:24.051 --> 38:26.721
but keep it a secret from my wife for now.

38:27.471 --> 38:28.472
And Seok-ryu.

38:29.765 --> 38:32.768
She'll cause a riot if she finds out.

38:34.186 --> 38:35.187
Yeah…

38:37.857 --> 38:38.691
[exhales]

38:42.028 --> 38:43.571
-How does it look?
-Bring it down.

38:43.654 --> 38:44.488
-Down?
-Yeah.

38:44.572 --> 38:45.823
It has to be seen from here.

38:45.906 --> 38:47.742
-[Jae-suk] That looks nice.
-[In-suk] Yeah.

38:49.452 --> 38:50.661
Who is it?

38:50.745 --> 38:51.662
[silence]

38:52.288 --> 38:53.956
Is she serious?

38:54.040 --> 38:55.624
♪ Chantto Baegi ♪

38:55.708 --> 38:57.168
You don't know Lee Chan-won?

38:57.251 --> 38:59.378
I haven't been in Korea for that long.

38:59.920 --> 39:02.340
-I guess he's cute.
-[Jae-suk] He's not just cute.

39:02.423 --> 39:05.760
Seriously, this one poster
really brightens up the place!

39:05.843 --> 39:06.969
My eyesight's improving too!

39:07.053 --> 39:08.804
It's practically her religion now.

39:08.888 --> 39:09.972
-Hallelujah!
-Hallelujah!

39:10.056 --> 39:11.974
-[Mi-suk] Merciful Buddha!
-[In-suk laughing]

39:12.058 --> 39:13.559
I get it.

39:13.642 --> 39:16.270
This piece of paper is much better
than my actual husband.

39:16.354 --> 39:17.688
-Of course.
-[Mi-suk] Why?

39:17.772 --> 39:19.899
-Did you fight with your husband again?
-Yeah.

39:19.982 --> 39:22.651
You know what? Only fight
if there's a chance of rehabilitation.

39:22.735 --> 39:25.863
I can't expect someone who never clears
his own dirty dishes to do anything.

39:25.946 --> 39:27.990
Does he eat all three meals at home?

39:28.074 --> 39:29.075
-Yeah!
-Goodness.

39:29.658 --> 39:31.744
-All three meals?
-That's right.

39:31.827 --> 39:32.912
-My goodness.
-[In-suk] Hey.

39:32.995 --> 39:36.540
I said, "Let's go out to eat," and he said
he hated the smell of foods with MSG.

39:36.624 --> 39:38.918
-[gasps]
-You know how much MSG I put in his soups?

39:39.001 --> 39:40.628
[all laughing]

39:40.711 --> 39:42.546
He's lucky it wasn't rat poison!

39:42.630 --> 39:43.464
I know!

39:43.547 --> 39:45.049
Husbands don't know that.

39:45.132 --> 39:46.384
[In-suk] They all don't.

39:46.467 --> 39:47.843
Maybe you don't add enough.

39:47.927 --> 39:49.720
I add a whole bunch in!

39:49.804 --> 39:50.846
[Hye-suk] Really?

39:50.930 --> 39:53.516
Gosh, I'm the most envious of Hye-suk.

39:54.058 --> 39:54.892
Why me?

39:54.975 --> 39:58.479
You both independently do your own work.
You live apart and are cool about it.

39:58.562 --> 40:00.898
It's so cool!

40:00.981 --> 40:03.317
-It is.
-I bet you two don't even fight.

40:03.401 --> 40:05.152
No, we don't fight.

40:05.236 --> 40:06.112
[In-suk chuckles]

40:06.195 --> 40:08.239
Hey, her family is
in a different world altogether.

40:08.322 --> 40:10.574
It's been hard
to even see my husband around lately.

40:10.658 --> 40:12.076
-Why?
-[Mi-suk] I don't know.

40:12.159 --> 40:13.911
I don't know. Who knows what he's up to?

40:13.994 --> 40:15.538
He always comes home at dawn.

40:15.621 --> 40:16.997
[Jae-suk] What? Dawn?

40:17.081 --> 40:18.666
He's staying out all night!

40:18.749 --> 40:21.710
Mi-suk, some men stay out
late enough to see the morning dew.

40:21.794 --> 40:23.712
-That's a serious problem!
-[Jae-suk] Of course!

40:23.796 --> 40:27.591
Why are you being so serious?
Forget it. It's not like that.

40:27.675 --> 40:29.427
-He has business--
-[Jae-suk] What business?

40:29.510 --> 40:31.178
Funerals, class reunions, and what else?

40:31.262 --> 40:33.639
-Yeah, those are the best excuses.
-Yeah!

40:33.722 --> 40:34.682
[In-suk] My goodness.

40:34.765 --> 40:37.935
Mi-suk, you need to be careful!

40:38.018 --> 40:40.271
He could be having an affair!

40:40.354 --> 40:42.231
What are you talking about?

40:42.940 --> 40:45.901
-[In-suk] Hey! What's wrong with you?
-[Jae-suk] Are you okay?

40:45.985 --> 40:47.486
-It got everywhere!
-Unbelievable.

40:47.570 --> 40:51.490
How many funerals did he go to?
One, two, three…

40:51.574 --> 40:53.033
He went to three funerals.

40:53.117 --> 40:54.326
Wipe your mouth.

40:54.410 --> 40:55.661
No, wait! Is that okay?

40:55.744 --> 40:57.329
-Is that a rag?
-[Jae-suk] It's a cloth.

40:57.413 --> 40:58.831
It doesn't smell. Wipe your mouth.

40:59.331 --> 41:02.334
[In-suk] That's right.
Is your shop taking a break?

41:02.418 --> 41:04.044
-[Hye-suk coughing]
-What?

41:04.128 --> 41:05.671
It hasn't been open for days.

41:05.754 --> 41:06.672
What?

41:06.755 --> 41:09.300
[In-suk] Hey, look into it quick. Okay?

41:10.050 --> 41:11.719
What are we going to do?

41:11.802 --> 41:13.387
[mysterious music playing]

41:24.857 --> 41:25.691
[exhales]

41:30.529 --> 41:31.447
[paper rustling]

41:40.581 --> 41:42.958
SHORT-TERM CREDIT LOAN
REVOLVING CREDIT

41:43.042 --> 41:46.170
[exclaims]

41:46.253 --> 41:48.464
[breathing heavily]

41:54.261 --> 41:55.179
[man slurping]

41:56.013 --> 41:57.097
[exclaims]

41:59.433 --> 42:00.434
Hello.

42:00.518 --> 42:02.102
Hi.

42:04.271 --> 42:05.272
[Dan-ho] Wait.

42:08.234 --> 42:10.152
There are two seats here.
Would you like to sit?

42:12.655 --> 42:13.656
Right.

42:16.825 --> 42:18.160
Thank you.

42:18.244 --> 42:21.038
Not at all.
It wasn't my chair to begin with.

42:22.456 --> 42:23.499
[grunts]

42:28.587 --> 42:29.421
[exhales]

42:33.801 --> 42:35.261
[sighs] Excuse me,

42:35.344 --> 42:37.721
I usually try not to interfere.

42:39.265 --> 42:41.600
But you shouldn't be here
while Yeon-du is home alone.

42:42.268 --> 42:43.269
Yeon-du…

42:45.354 --> 42:47.314
went to an overnight camp
for kindergarteners.

42:47.898 --> 42:48.774
I see…

42:50.901 --> 42:53.320
-She went to camp.
-[Dan-ho] Yes.

42:55.489 --> 42:56.323
I'm sorry.

42:58.534 --> 42:59.827
It's fine.

43:00.995 --> 43:01.954
But…

43:02.997 --> 43:04.665
you're having dinner pretty late.

43:04.748 --> 43:05.749
Yes.

43:06.542 --> 43:09.211
I was out on a call and had to
go around looking for hospitals.

43:10.087 --> 43:12.047
Did the hospital refuse a patient?

43:12.131 --> 43:13.507
Yeah.

43:13.591 --> 43:14.842
I'm sure you know,

43:14.925 --> 43:17.595
but there's a lot of patients
and a shortage of medical staff.

43:17.678 --> 43:19.430
That's the current situation.

43:19.513 --> 43:21.390
What happened to the patient?

43:21.473 --> 43:24.893
I made sure the patient
was examined and admitted.

43:25.644 --> 43:27.479
[exhales] I'm relieved to hear that.

43:32.234 --> 43:33.777
You're really impressive.

43:33.861 --> 43:35.154
Excuse me?

43:35.821 --> 43:37.072
What gives?

43:37.156 --> 43:39.575
Is this a "love your enemy" type of thing?

43:39.658 --> 43:40.701
[chuckles]

43:40.784 --> 43:45.164
It's not that. You know how to give
honest criticism in a kind way.

43:46.999 --> 43:50.419
I hope you'll continue
to look after Yeon-du.

43:51.837 --> 43:54.256
Tell her to give me another chance.

43:54.923 --> 43:58.510
If you've said anything bad about me,
I ask that you take it back.

43:58.594 --> 44:01.430
I didn't do anything like that at all.

44:02.389 --> 44:03.390
Okay, then.

44:05.517 --> 44:06.685
By the way…

44:08.395 --> 44:09.855
If you don't mind me asking,

44:11.315 --> 44:12.900
but does Yeon-du have any other family?

44:13.484 --> 44:14.360
Oh.

44:15.527 --> 44:17.696
Yeon-du's mom is very far away.

44:18.656 --> 44:19.490
[Mo-eum] I see.

44:26.121 --> 44:28.540
I think you're a really good dad.

44:29.583 --> 44:31.377
[pleasant music playing]

44:31.460 --> 44:32.544
Me?

44:32.628 --> 44:33.629
Yes.

44:35.172 --> 44:36.715
You raised your daughter well.

44:37.383 --> 44:40.177
Look at how smart and cute she is.

44:43.222 --> 44:44.223
Right?

44:45.641 --> 44:47.101
Isn't she cute?

44:49.395 --> 44:52.106
She's the most precious person
in the world to me.

44:53.607 --> 44:59.738
I could give everything up for her.

45:00.406 --> 45:01.490
Everything.

45:03.200 --> 45:04.368
Don't give anything up.

45:07.037 --> 45:08.247
Well…

45:10.207 --> 45:12.042
My dad passed away when I was young.

45:14.336 --> 45:15.712
So I know what it's like.

45:16.422 --> 45:19.049
If my mom ever sacrificed
anything for me,

45:19.133 --> 45:21.176
I hated that the most.

45:24.721 --> 45:26.640
I'm just saying.

45:29.226 --> 45:32.688
Then, can I play with Yeon-du
from time to time again?

45:33.981 --> 45:35.649
Of course,

45:35.732 --> 45:37.234
as long as it's okay with her.

45:37.317 --> 45:38.569
Really?

45:38.652 --> 45:41.905
Thank you. Can you tell me what she likes?

45:41.989 --> 45:43.282
I want to win her back.

45:44.158 --> 45:46.660
-What does Yeon-du like?
-[Mo-eum] Yes.

45:46.743 --> 45:51.373
[slurring] She liked ghosts
and zombies in the past.

45:51.457 --> 45:53.834
What? You're starting to slur…

45:53.917 --> 45:56.545
Isn't good pronunciation
important to news reporters?

45:56.628 --> 45:57.546
[quirky music playing]

45:57.629 --> 46:01.175
[slurring] Yeon-du likes aliens.
She likes aliens.

46:06.346 --> 46:07.347
Dan-ho?

46:07.890 --> 46:08.891
[groans softly]

46:08.974 --> 46:12.186
How much can you usually drink?

46:12.269 --> 46:13.395
What?

46:14.521 --> 46:16.190
[chuckles softly]

46:18.317 --> 46:20.027
One can of beer.

46:20.110 --> 46:22.779
What he's saying and doing don't line up.

46:23.906 --> 46:25.824
Goodness.

46:27.743 --> 46:29.328
Dan-ho? What do I do?

46:29.953 --> 46:31.163
Goodness!

46:32.164 --> 46:34.374
Assisting a drunk person home.

46:34.458 --> 46:36.752
This is off-the-clock work!

46:38.795 --> 46:42.466
If he weren't Yeon-du's dad,
I would've just left him.

46:42.549 --> 46:43.467
[grunts]

46:44.551 --> 46:48.263
Dan-ho, I don't think
you should drink for a while.

46:49.056 --> 46:51.391
Just stick to the Pine Ear Drink! Got it?

46:52.059 --> 46:53.393
[straining]

46:56.605 --> 46:57.439
[groans]

46:58.732 --> 46:59.566
[exhales]

47:01.735 --> 47:02.569
[groans]

47:03.654 --> 47:07.658
[panting] I'm sure
he won't freeze to death, right?

47:21.213 --> 47:22.047
[door opens]

47:23.131 --> 47:23.966
[door closes]

47:35.769 --> 47:36.812
[music ends]

47:43.402 --> 47:45.821
-[breathing heavily]
-[Geun-sik] Are you insane?

47:45.904 --> 47:49.408
Is this how you treat someone
after a hard day's work?

47:49.491 --> 47:52.411
A hard day's work? You were working?

47:52.494 --> 47:55.205
Where did you go off gallivanting
after closing the shop?

47:55.956 --> 47:57.791
What on earth have you been up to?

48:00.377 --> 48:02.296
You applied for revolving credit?

48:02.379 --> 48:04.256
You took out a cash advance?

48:06.091 --> 48:08.552
Hey, you have eyes. Look at this.

48:09.303 --> 48:11.096
The bean sprouts were on sale
for 1,500 won.

48:11.179 --> 48:12.848
The pork belly cost 9,900 won.

48:12.931 --> 48:14.933
The gas bill is 3,180 won!

48:15.017 --> 48:16.643
[breathing heavily]

48:16.727 --> 48:21.481
I keep track of these trivial details
as we've tightened our belts.

48:22.858 --> 48:23.900
How could you?

48:24.985 --> 48:26.570
How could you mess up again?

48:26.653 --> 48:28.030
[Seok-ryu] I'm home.

48:28.822 --> 48:29.823
[door closes]

48:32.159 --> 48:35.203
-Mom, what's wrong?
-I can't put up with your dad anymore.

48:35.287 --> 48:36.288
I'm at my limit.

48:36.371 --> 48:38.624
What's wrong? Dad, what is it?

48:38.707 --> 48:40.167
No, it's nothing.

48:40.250 --> 48:42.836
[Mi-suk] You close the shop
and stay out all night!

48:42.919 --> 48:45.756
And you messed up with money again!

48:48.050 --> 48:49.635
Tell me why.

48:50.260 --> 48:52.179
Did you co-sign another friend's loan?

48:52.262 --> 48:53.930
No.

48:54.014 --> 48:54.848
Wait…

48:55.891 --> 48:57.017
Were you gambling?

48:57.100 --> 48:58.435
No, it's not like that.

48:58.518 --> 48:59.394
Then…

49:00.062 --> 49:02.230
-Are you having an affair?
-Honey!

49:03.398 --> 49:05.275
You really don't trust me?

49:05.359 --> 49:07.277
How can I trust you
when you act like this?

49:07.361 --> 49:09.946
How could you say… [sniffles]

49:10.530 --> 49:13.992
How can you back me
into a corner like this every time?

49:15.786 --> 49:17.412
I had no choice…

49:18.955 --> 49:20.916
I had no other choice but to do that.

49:21.541 --> 49:23.001
[breath trembling]

49:23.085 --> 49:25.379
Dad, what is it? What's going on?

49:26.713 --> 49:28.173
There was an accident.

49:34.846 --> 49:36.473
Excuse me, sir?

49:36.556 --> 49:38.850
-Yes?
-[water running]

49:38.934 --> 49:39.935
[dramatic music playing]

49:40.018 --> 49:41.436
[chuckles] What is it?

49:41.520 --> 49:43.397
I think something's in the food.

49:43.480 --> 49:45.691
I think it's a hair.
You should take a look.

49:47.776 --> 49:49.194
That's not possible.

49:49.903 --> 49:51.488
-[boy 1 yelps]
-[Geun-sik groans]

49:51.571 --> 49:53.073
-I'm so sorry!
-[boy 2] Seriously?

49:53.156 --> 49:54.074
Were you burned?

49:54.157 --> 49:54.991
[boy 1 groans]

49:55.075 --> 49:57.619
Let me see.
You should've been more careful!

49:58.620 --> 50:01.915
-I'm sorry. Let's go to the hospital.
-Let go of me! [yelps]

50:04.042 --> 50:06.378
I'm just worried you're really hurt.

50:06.461 --> 50:08.255
Of course, I'm hurt!

50:08.338 --> 50:10.173
I'm hurt, and my watch…

50:10.257 --> 50:11.508
[gasps]

50:13.301 --> 50:14.636
My watch stopped.

50:15.804 --> 50:17.764
-Watch?
-[boy 1] Come on!

50:18.390 --> 50:20.726
The watch… I'm sorry.

50:22.644 --> 50:26.148
Are you trying to brush this off
with just an apology?

50:27.065 --> 50:29.609
That watch costs 30 million won!

50:29.693 --> 50:31.194
It does?

50:31.778 --> 50:34.239
[boy 2] No. It costs way more, mister.

50:34.322 --> 50:37.451
Do you think you can buy
this watch with just money?

50:37.534 --> 50:40.495
To buy this, you need to
build a purchase history

50:40.579 --> 50:42.581
by buying several items from this brand.

50:42.664 --> 50:44.958
It's a top-of-the-line luxury brand.

50:46.042 --> 50:47.794
That means…

50:48.295 --> 50:51.381
even if I sold you off, I still
won't be able to afford this watch.

50:51.465 --> 50:53.091
Don't try to touch it.

50:56.261 --> 50:58.388
Okay, I understand.

51:00.056 --> 51:04.102
I'll cover the cost of repairs then.

51:04.186 --> 51:07.522
Hey, he kills my precious watch
and wants to cover the cost of repairs.

51:07.647 --> 51:08.774
[both chuckle]

51:08.857 --> 51:11.359
Look, the thing about this watch is

51:11.443 --> 51:13.153
he bought it less than a week ago.

51:13.236 --> 51:15.614
It's totally brand new.

51:16.323 --> 51:17.532
Then, what should I…

51:17.616 --> 51:19.743
Reimburse the full amount
before I sue you!

51:19.826 --> 51:21.369
-You're so frustrating.
-Gosh.

51:22.329 --> 51:23.371
Sir…

51:39.971 --> 51:44.434
DESIGNATED DRIVERS

51:46.394 --> 51:47.479
[phone ringing]

51:50.398 --> 51:53.610
[automated voice] You have been assigned.
Proceed to the pickup location.

51:57.948 --> 52:00.867
Sir, did you call for a designated driver?

52:00.951 --> 52:02.869
-[man] Yeah.
-[Geun-sik] Okay. [groans]

52:03.787 --> 52:04.955
I'm sorry.

52:05.622 --> 52:06.623
This way, sir.

52:14.422 --> 52:17.801
Sir, we're at the location you provided.

52:17.884 --> 52:20.887
Sir, we're here.

52:21.513 --> 52:24.015
-[man retching]
-[Geun-sik groans] Sir!

52:26.685 --> 52:28.353
-Sir!
-[man groans]

52:28.436 --> 52:31.231
-Sweetie, why are you so cute?
-[Geun-sik] Yes?

52:31.314 --> 52:34.067
-Where's your car?
-Car? Is it here?

52:34.150 --> 52:35.443
Over there!

52:36.236 --> 52:38.405
Do you want to come over?

52:38.488 --> 52:40.532
-[Geun-sik] Where do you live?
-My house?

52:42.450 --> 52:45.203
Ma'am, we're here.

52:45.287 --> 52:47.455
-[car lock beeps]
-Here's your key.

52:48.874 --> 52:50.542
You're so annoying.

52:51.167 --> 52:52.377
[Geun-sik] Take care, ma'am.

52:59.009 --> 52:59.843
[exhales]

53:07.183 --> 53:08.810
[line ringing]

53:08.894 --> 53:10.812
Hello, it's me.

53:11.396 --> 53:13.398
I deposited 20 million won just now.

53:13.773 --> 53:15.150
Please accept this for now.

53:15.233 --> 53:17.819
I'll try to get the rest somehow.

53:17.903 --> 53:20.363
Just give me a few more days.

53:23.158 --> 53:26.620
So to pay them, you took money
from our living expense account?

53:27.203 --> 53:28.747
You took out a credit card loan

53:29.289 --> 53:30.415
and worked as a driver?

53:31.541 --> 53:33.627
[scoffs] To handle that alone…

53:33.710 --> 53:35.128
Are you a fool?

53:35.962 --> 53:37.756
Do you have any sense at all?

53:37.839 --> 53:40.008
You do think I'm a fool.

53:41.843 --> 53:44.512
You look down on me for being incompetent.

53:46.473 --> 53:47.390
When did I ever?

53:47.474 --> 53:49.726
Well, all the time.

53:50.977 --> 53:52.562
With me, it's always money.

53:54.522 --> 53:56.274
All you ever talk to me about is money.

53:57.150 --> 53:58.276
[exhales]

53:58.360 --> 54:00.487
But gosh,
if I were to tell you about this,

54:00.570 --> 54:02.072
what would you think of me then?

54:03.782 --> 54:05.742
What if I got sued
and had to close the shop?

54:05.825 --> 54:09.162
If I lost even the tiny bit of income

54:09.245 --> 54:10.622
that I'm earning now,

54:11.706 --> 54:13.708
what would that make me?

54:14.834 --> 54:16.670
The only thing I know how to do…

54:18.546 --> 54:19.464
[sniffles]

54:21.967 --> 54:24.177
All I know how to do
is just make tteokbokki.

54:25.095 --> 54:27.889
If I can't even do that,
then what does that make me?

54:27.973 --> 54:29.015
[emotional music playing]

54:29.099 --> 54:32.602
Well? What can I
contribute to this family?

54:32.686 --> 54:34.688
There's nothing else in my life.

54:34.771 --> 54:36.523
Dad…

54:37.482 --> 54:41.027
I'll do whatever I can
to pay that money back.

54:41.611 --> 54:43.238
Who asked you to?

54:43.321 --> 54:48.451
-That's not what's important right now--
-Please, Mi-suk. Stop scolding me!

54:49.202 --> 54:52.706
It hurts when I'm hit too, you know.

54:53.331 --> 54:55.000
Okay? It hurts me too.

54:56.334 --> 54:57.293
I'll be home later.

55:04.634 --> 55:06.052
-[door opens]
-[scoffs]

55:06.970 --> 55:08.680
-[door closes]
-[crying]

55:09.180 --> 55:10.265
Mom.

55:13.435 --> 55:14.269
[Mi-suk crying]

55:28.033 --> 55:29.159
[Seok-ryu] Dad!

55:29.242 --> 55:31.453
-[Geun-sik] Hey, why did you…
-[thuds]

55:31.536 --> 55:32.787
Are you okay?

55:34.622 --> 55:35.957
[Seok-ryu exhales]

55:39.836 --> 55:41.504
[Geun-sik whimpering]

55:47.218 --> 55:48.553
Dad.

55:48.636 --> 55:49.971
[Geun-sik] I'm okay.

55:50.764 --> 55:52.015
I'm all right. [sniffles]

55:55.852 --> 55:58.354
You always did this for me
when I was a kid.

55:59.314 --> 56:01.524
Now, I'm doing it for you.

56:02.484 --> 56:04.152
I've grown up a lot, haven't I?

56:11.701 --> 56:13.286
I'm sorry, Seok-ryu.

56:13.369 --> 56:15.080
Why would you be sorry?

56:15.663 --> 56:16.873
They're the bad guys.

56:17.457 --> 56:19.167
Let's just go to the cops.

56:19.250 --> 56:21.753
Full compensation is ridiculous.

56:21.836 --> 56:23.338
We can't report it.

56:24.089 --> 56:28.301
They could close our shop
for violating the Food Sanitation Act.

56:28.384 --> 56:29.511
[exhales]

56:31.513 --> 56:35.600
[chuckles softly]
I have no right to be a father, do I?

56:36.392 --> 56:38.853
Gosh, I have a beautiful daughter,

56:39.437 --> 56:41.731
but I've never bought you a nice outfit.

56:43.191 --> 56:46.277
I couldn't even send you any allowance
when you were studying overseas.

56:48.238 --> 56:49.489
And I'm still…

56:51.032 --> 56:52.784
causing you to worry over money.

56:54.744 --> 56:58.498
How can you place value on that
with money? It should be with love.

57:00.125 --> 57:01.835
What about me? I'm unemployed.

57:01.918 --> 57:03.795
I don't have the right
to be your daughter?

57:03.878 --> 57:05.839
What are you talking about?

57:05.922 --> 57:07.257
Hey! You're…

57:08.299 --> 57:11.177
You'll always have the right
to be my daughter.

57:11.261 --> 57:14.389
No renewal is needed,
and it can't be cancelled.

57:15.014 --> 57:18.268
You'll always be my daughter, okay?

57:18.852 --> 57:20.603
It's the same for me.

57:21.354 --> 57:24.441
Bae Geun-sik will always be my dad.

57:29.279 --> 57:30.363
[chuckles]

57:42.167 --> 57:43.501
BLACKMAILERS
POLICE STATION

57:45.086 --> 57:46.754
BAD GUYS

57:48.840 --> 57:51.092
-[inhales]
-[scribbling]

57:51.843 --> 57:53.553
We can't report it.

57:54.220 --> 57:57.891
They could close our shop
for violating the Food Sanitation Act.

57:57.974 --> 58:00.852
Damn it, I can't do this or that.

58:00.935 --> 58:02.687
I'm going to lose my mind.

58:06.399 --> 58:07.484
[inhales]

58:07.567 --> 58:11.529
Fish cake soup, hair, watch.

58:16.201 --> 58:18.536
If only we had
security cameras in the shop…

58:22.040 --> 58:23.291
Security camera!

58:26.961 --> 58:28.588
BEST CLEANERS

58:32.258 --> 58:33.510
Hello!

58:34.260 --> 58:36.221
Hey, Seok-ryu!

58:36.304 --> 58:38.306
-Are you dropping off clothes?
-No.

58:38.389 --> 58:41.559
Can I see some footage
from your security camera?

58:41.643 --> 58:44.229
-You want to see too?
-Did someone else come by?

58:44.312 --> 58:45.813
Seung-hyo already came by for it.

58:46.606 --> 58:47.857
What's going on?

58:49.734 --> 58:50.610
[phone vibrating]

58:50.693 --> 58:52.820
BAE SEOK-RYU

58:52.904 --> 58:55.073
[lounge music playing in background]

58:55.657 --> 58:58.368
-Are you the son of Root Diner's owner?
-Yes.

58:59.786 --> 59:01.496
Is the burn on your hand okay?

59:01.579 --> 59:02.789
Of course not.

59:03.498 --> 59:06.125
Let's resolve the watch issue first.
We'll discuss this later.

59:06.209 --> 59:07.210
Okay.

59:07.752 --> 59:11.130
First, take the remaining money.

59:12.173 --> 59:13.007
[sniffles]

59:13.591 --> 59:15.969
Your father said
he couldn't get the money.

59:16.052 --> 59:18.429
You must've worked hard for this.

59:19.055 --> 59:21.099
[Seung-hyo] I'm sorry,
but before you take it,

59:21.182 --> 59:23.851
could I see the watch my father broke?

59:25.061 --> 59:26.729
The watch? Why?

59:26.813 --> 59:28.565
Since we're covering the full cost,

59:28.648 --> 59:30.358
I'd like to at least see

59:30.441 --> 59:32.318
what this expensive watch looks like.

59:32.402 --> 59:34.320
-I'm sure he does.
-[chuckles softly]

59:34.404 --> 59:36.447
Yeah, okay.

59:36.531 --> 59:38.950
He'll never be able
to afford it himself.

59:39.909 --> 59:43.162
So this is the watch. Wow.

59:43.246 --> 59:46.040
This is an Audemar
Constantine Philip Mills.

59:46.124 --> 59:47.834
He must've heard of it before.

59:47.917 --> 59:51.087
Of course. It's one of the top
luxury watches in the world.

59:51.170 --> 59:52.297
Wow…

59:53.256 --> 59:54.841
I have the same watch.

59:55.425 --> 59:56.759
What?

59:58.344 --> 59:59.637
How interesting.

59:59.721 --> 01:00:02.473
I received an award recently.

01:00:02.557 --> 01:00:05.893
This watch company sponsored the awards
and gave me one as a gift.

01:00:05.977 --> 01:00:07.562
[amusing music playing]

01:00:07.645 --> 01:00:09.814
This is a new model that just came out.

01:00:09.897 --> 01:00:12.442
The serial number starts with 245D.

01:00:13.401 --> 01:00:17.488
But… this one doesn't.

01:00:18.281 --> 01:00:19.574
It starts with 215D.

01:00:20.617 --> 01:00:22.118
-It's different?
-I don't know.

01:00:22.201 --> 01:00:25.413
This chronograph is so crude.

01:00:25.496 --> 01:00:27.957
And why does the blue dial look so dull?

01:00:28.958 --> 01:00:31.878
The stainless steel
should've been brush finished.

01:00:31.961 --> 01:00:34.130
Why is it so shiny?

01:00:34.922 --> 01:00:39.093
Goodness.
This is just a cheap knock-off.

01:00:39.844 --> 01:00:41.179
Where did you get this?

01:00:41.262 --> 01:00:42.597
What would you even know?

01:00:50.188 --> 01:00:51.981
[Seung-hyo] Do you know where that is?

01:00:53.316 --> 01:00:55.860
It would be nice
if we could zoom there a little.

01:00:55.943 --> 01:00:58.112
Yes. Just like that. [snaps fingers]

01:00:58.196 --> 01:01:01.449
Hey, what is this? Who are you?

01:01:01.532 --> 01:01:03.451
No, let's keep watching. It gets better.

01:01:03.534 --> 01:01:04.577
Okay.

01:01:06.329 --> 01:01:09.123
[Seung-hyo] I see. That's how?

01:01:12.418 --> 01:01:14.253
Wow.

01:01:16.589 --> 01:01:18.883
You prepared the foreign object
and put it in the soup.

01:01:19.676 --> 01:01:21.427
You called the owner over

01:01:21.511 --> 01:01:23.471
and deliberately spilled
the soup on your watch.

01:01:23.554 --> 01:01:24.722
Wow.

01:01:25.848 --> 01:01:27.141
You must've practiced a lot.

01:01:28.184 --> 01:01:29.185
And?

01:01:29.852 --> 01:01:32.563
That video isn't proof
that we put something in the food.

01:01:32.647 --> 01:01:33.481
[boy 1] Yeah.

01:01:33.564 --> 01:01:36.484
We recorded everything.
The hair and the damaged watch!

01:01:36.567 --> 01:01:37.443
Proof?

01:01:38.277 --> 01:01:39.237
I'm glad you said that.

01:01:39.946 --> 01:01:42.990
You see the time stamp on the footage?
It says 11:59 a.m.

01:01:43.074 --> 01:01:44.200
Take a look.

01:01:44.283 --> 01:01:49.789
This means when you went into the shop,
it was at least after 12 p.m.

01:01:49.872 --> 01:01:56.421
So why is your broken watch
stopped at 11:45?

01:01:56.504 --> 01:01:57.338
Why is that?

01:01:57.422 --> 01:02:00.049
-[whispering] You should've checked it.
-Shut up.

01:02:00.133 --> 01:02:02.677
[Dan-ho in normal voice]
Hello. Sorry I'm late.

01:02:02.760 --> 01:02:04.721
What took you so long? I was waiting.

01:02:04.804 --> 01:02:06.431
Who's this guy?

01:02:06.514 --> 01:02:07.807
Are you working with him?

01:02:09.016 --> 01:02:10.435
Let me introduce myself.

01:02:11.978 --> 01:02:13.688
I'm Kang Dan-ho
with The Chungwoo Daily.

01:02:15.565 --> 01:02:16.733
THE CHUNGWOO DAILY
KANG DAN-HO

01:02:16.816 --> 01:02:19.026
I've really wanted to meet you two.

01:02:19.610 --> 01:02:21.738
I received a tip from someone.

01:02:24.073 --> 01:02:26.200
Why is the quality
of this footage so good?

01:02:26.743 --> 01:02:29.078
A lot of thieves have stolen clothes
from the dry cleaner.

01:02:29.162 --> 01:02:31.539
-So he installed the best camera model.
-I see.

01:02:32.206 --> 01:02:33.875
[Seung-hyo]
That's not what's important.

01:02:33.958 --> 01:02:36.461
I used this photo to try
and identify these two.

01:02:36.544 --> 01:02:37.378
Right.

01:02:37.462 --> 01:02:41.048
They claimed they had NerTube channel
with 100,000 subscribers.

01:02:41.132 --> 01:02:42.175
But that was a lie.

01:02:43.050 --> 01:02:46.971
Here. They have an empty channel
with 30 subscribers.

01:02:47.972 --> 01:02:49.724
They likely use it as bait for blackmail.

01:02:49.807 --> 01:02:53.060
Yeah, I'm sure there are
other victims of the same con.

01:02:54.020 --> 01:02:55.062
[Dan-ho] I think so too.

01:02:55.730 --> 01:02:57.148
They're probably older…

01:02:57.231 --> 01:02:59.650
Unfamiliar with NerTube…

01:02:59.734 --> 01:03:01.194
Small business owners.

01:03:05.031 --> 01:03:06.115
[both exclaiming]

01:03:06.949 --> 01:03:09.243
[boy 1] What are you doing? Hey!

01:03:09.327 --> 01:03:10.161
See? I knew it.

01:03:10.244 --> 01:03:12.079
The burn on your hand was a lie too.

01:03:13.873 --> 01:03:16.709
The owner spilled soup on his hand too,
but he was fine.

01:03:17.418 --> 01:03:20.296
[Dan-ho] I looked into it,
and there were similar incidents nearby.

01:03:20.379 --> 01:03:22.340
Despicable crimes that prey

01:03:22.423 --> 01:03:25.468
on the weak and powerless
because they can't touch big franchises.

01:03:26.052 --> 01:03:30.807
[Seung-hyo] Most recently, I heard a watch
stopped working at a gomtang restaurant.

01:03:31.974 --> 01:03:36.187
[sniffs] I think I can smell
ox bone soup from the strap.

01:03:36.270 --> 01:03:38.314
-[sniffing]
-[Seung-hyo] Ma'am?

01:03:38.940 --> 01:03:40.274
Yes, Seung-hyo?

01:03:40.358 --> 01:03:44.612
I'm sorry. I should call you
President Choi now, right?

01:03:44.695 --> 01:03:46.531
Thanks for lending us the projector.

01:03:47.824 --> 01:03:50.535
Their faces
are being recorded on camera, right?

01:03:52.453 --> 01:03:53.579
Of course!

01:03:54.413 --> 01:03:55.790
[laughing nervously]

01:03:57.458 --> 01:03:58.584
We're screwed.

01:03:59.335 --> 01:04:00.753
[intense music playing]

01:04:01.504 --> 01:04:02.672
[Seung-hyo] Dan-ho!

01:04:04.757 --> 01:04:06.050
Wait for me!

01:04:07.510 --> 01:04:09.136
-[boy 2] Call me later!
-[boy 1] Okay!

01:04:17.436 --> 01:04:18.354
[Seung-hyo grunts]

01:04:23.943 --> 01:04:25.236
[boy] Let go of me!

01:04:26.070 --> 01:04:26.904
Ow.

01:04:28.030 --> 01:04:30.199
[grunting]

01:04:32.118 --> 01:04:32.994
[chuckling]

01:04:34.871 --> 01:04:35.955
[boy exclaiming]

01:04:37.290 --> 01:04:38.958
Why is he so fast?

01:04:42.753 --> 01:04:45.006
Hey, you expect to get a story
at this rate?

01:04:45.089 --> 01:04:46.215
[groans softly]

01:04:46.299 --> 01:04:47.133
[thuds]

01:04:47.884 --> 01:04:48.718
Goodness.

01:04:49.302 --> 01:04:50.303
[panting]

01:04:51.429 --> 01:04:53.055
Watch out.

01:04:57.518 --> 01:04:59.896
[panting] Are you okay? Hey.

01:05:03.149 --> 01:05:04.483
Hey.

01:05:11.324 --> 01:05:12.742
[horn honking]

01:05:13.534 --> 01:05:14.368
[panting]

01:05:14.827 --> 01:05:15.912
Damn it.

01:05:15.995 --> 01:05:16.913
[exclaiming]

01:05:18.497 --> 01:05:19.624
[exclaims in frustration]

01:05:20.958 --> 01:05:21.876
[boy exclaims]

01:05:22.543 --> 01:05:23.377
[scoffs]

01:05:24.629 --> 01:05:25.588
[Seok-ryu] Hey.

01:05:26.422 --> 01:05:28.507
[both grunting]

01:05:29.133 --> 01:05:30.009
[panting]

01:05:30.092 --> 01:05:32.178
How dare you do that to my dad?

01:05:33.220 --> 01:05:34.221
[shrieks]

01:05:35.473 --> 01:05:37.141
-[groans]
-Who in the world are you?

01:05:37.725 --> 01:05:39.268
Damn it.

01:05:39.352 --> 01:05:40.853
[groaning]

01:05:40.937 --> 01:05:41.938
[breathing heavily]

01:05:43.356 --> 01:05:45.358
Hey, is your head okay?

01:05:45.441 --> 01:05:47.610
-Are you hurt?
-[Seok-ryu] I'm okay. I'm not hurt.

01:05:48.611 --> 01:05:50.196
[Seung-hyo] Hey, your nose is bleeding…

01:05:51.405 --> 01:05:52.740
That bastard.

01:05:52.823 --> 01:05:55.076
Hey, this isn't because of him.

01:05:55.159 --> 01:05:57.411
I overdid it the past few days.
I'm just tired.

01:05:59.580 --> 01:06:01.624
Hey, stop the blood with this.

01:06:01.707 --> 01:06:03.584
You'll get blood on it.
Isn't it expensive?

01:06:03.668 --> 01:06:04.835
That's not important.

01:06:04.919 --> 01:06:07.004
Why would you come here? It's dangerous.

01:06:07.088 --> 01:06:09.382
[Seok-ryu] What about you?
You just got your cast off

01:06:09.465 --> 01:06:11.968
and you're out here doing flying kicks.

01:06:12.051 --> 01:06:13.260
[Seung-hyo] Seriously?

01:06:18.432 --> 01:06:19.350
Jeez!

01:06:19.433 --> 01:06:23.270
-You the jerk who took my dad's money?
-Yeah, that's him.

01:06:23.354 --> 01:06:25.982
Uphold our family's honor
and get revenge.

01:06:26.065 --> 01:06:28.275
No! I think there's been
a misunderstanding.

01:06:28.359 --> 01:06:29.235
Kill him!

01:06:29.318 --> 01:06:30.444
[menacing music playing]

01:06:30.528 --> 01:06:31.946
-[grunts]
-[shrieks]

01:06:32.613 --> 01:06:33.531
[screaming]

01:06:34.448 --> 01:06:35.282
[music ends]

01:06:35.366 --> 01:06:36.283
What?

01:06:37.284 --> 01:06:39.286
You caught them?

01:06:42.456 --> 01:06:46.419
Okay, I'll be right there.

01:06:46.502 --> 01:06:48.337
-I'm coming right now.
-[call disconnects]

01:06:48.421 --> 01:06:50.047
Who was it? What did they say?

01:06:50.131 --> 01:06:52.466
They caught the men who blackmailed me.

01:06:53.134 --> 01:06:56.887
They were con artists.

01:07:00.224 --> 01:07:02.184
Honey, I'm going to the police station.

01:07:02.268 --> 01:07:03.519
[grunting]

01:07:03.602 --> 01:07:04.437
What are you doing?

01:07:04.520 --> 01:07:05.938
-[grunting]
-[whimpering]

01:07:06.480 --> 01:07:07.648
Why are you hitting me?

01:07:07.732 --> 01:07:09.692
[crying] Does it hurt? Does it?

01:07:10.276 --> 01:07:11.777
-[Geun-sik grunts]
-You deserve more!

01:07:12.486 --> 01:07:13.779
Honey…

01:07:13.863 --> 01:07:15.156
What was that?

01:07:16.032 --> 01:07:17.283
Just tteokbokki?

01:07:18.451 --> 01:07:20.244
The only thing I know how to do…

01:07:20.327 --> 01:07:21.370
[mellow music playing]

01:07:24.331 --> 01:07:26.375
All I know how to do
is just make tteokbokki.

01:07:27.376 --> 01:07:30.004
If I can't even do that,
then what does that make me?

01:07:31.422 --> 01:07:34.842
Well? What can I
contribute to this family?

01:07:34.925 --> 01:07:37.470
There's nothing else in my life.

01:07:37.553 --> 01:07:39.680
Don't you know
how special that tteokbokki is?

01:07:39.764 --> 01:07:41.557
You've spent decades in front of a stove.

01:07:42.475 --> 01:07:45.311
We raised our kids on that precious food.

01:07:45.394 --> 01:07:46.979
What do you mean it's just tteokbokki?

01:07:47.063 --> 01:07:48.230
How could you say that?

01:07:48.314 --> 01:07:50.691
[voice shaking] Mi-suk… [sniffles]

01:07:50.775 --> 01:07:52.526
[Mi-suk] There's nothing in your life?

01:07:52.610 --> 01:07:53.861
Then, what about us?

01:07:54.487 --> 01:07:57.990
Do I, Seok-ryu,
and Dong-jin mean nothing to you?

01:07:58.074 --> 01:08:01.786
[voice shaking] No,
you all mean everything to me.

01:08:01.869 --> 01:08:04.622
You're all too good for me.

01:08:04.705 --> 01:08:08.542
I'm not even wishing for anything big now.

01:08:09.043 --> 01:08:13.964
I just want to take care of our family
and make them happy. [crying]

01:08:16.592 --> 01:08:19.136
But it's so hard.

01:08:19.845 --> 01:08:22.389
Why is it so hard
to live an ordinary life?

01:08:22.973 --> 01:08:24.725
That's the greatest dream of all.

01:08:25.518 --> 01:08:27.728
It's the most meaningful
and valuable dream.

01:08:28.521 --> 01:08:32.358
But you know dreams come true, right?

01:08:34.318 --> 01:08:35.528
Mi-suk, I'm sorry.

01:08:36.904 --> 01:08:38.697
And thank you.

01:08:39.281 --> 01:08:40.950
Come here. [crying]

01:08:43.077 --> 01:08:44.411
As long as you get it, it's fine.

01:08:45.663 --> 01:08:46.956
So stop crying now.

01:08:48.290 --> 01:08:49.750
Let's go to the station.

01:08:49.834 --> 01:08:50.793
You're going too?

01:08:50.876 --> 01:08:53.462
Of course. Wherever we go,
we'll go together.

01:08:54.046 --> 01:08:56.465
We'll go on picnics
and see flowers on nice days.

01:08:57.049 --> 01:08:58.801
If we're sick,
we'll visit the hospital.

01:08:59.343 --> 01:09:01.262
Whether it's Heaven, Hell,

01:09:01.345 --> 01:09:03.305
or wherever the heavens send us,

01:09:03.389 --> 01:09:05.599
we'll go together in the afterlife.

01:09:05.683 --> 01:09:06.809
[chuckles softly]

01:09:08.018 --> 01:09:09.687
Because I'm your wife.

01:09:10.980 --> 01:09:11.939
And we're a family.

01:09:12.022 --> 01:09:15.317
Okay. Let's go together.

01:09:15.442 --> 01:09:17.486
-[sniffles] Okay. Let's go.
-Wait.

01:09:17.570 --> 01:09:19.697
Let me take this. I'll kill those jerks.

01:09:19.780 --> 01:09:20.698
-Honey.
-What?

01:09:20.781 --> 01:09:22.449
You'll end up in jail.

01:09:23.159 --> 01:09:24.243
You won't go with me?

01:09:24.326 --> 01:09:25.619
Honey, I love you.

01:09:26.579 --> 01:09:29.415
-I need those!
-[Geun-sik] There's no time. Let's go.

01:09:30.833 --> 01:09:33.294
HYEREUNG POLICE STATION

01:09:33.377 --> 01:09:35.546
-[sirens wailing in distance]
-[phone vibrating]

01:09:36.297 --> 01:09:37.131
[exhales]

01:09:37.756 --> 01:09:38.757
My dad's coming.

01:09:39.592 --> 01:09:40.676
Okay.

01:09:42.595 --> 01:09:47.141
I'll have this dry-cleaned
and give it back to you.

01:09:47.224 --> 01:09:48.767
Forget it. Just throw it away.

01:09:48.851 --> 01:09:51.854
You have money to burn?
You can't throw it away.

01:09:52.479 --> 01:09:53.856
It won't take long.

01:09:54.440 --> 01:09:55.566
Do whatever you want.

01:09:57.193 --> 01:09:58.611
Thanks for today.

01:09:59.778 --> 01:10:02.448
I didn't even know
that was happening to my dad.

01:10:03.532 --> 01:10:06.285
I was so happy
about finding what I wanted to do.

01:10:06.368 --> 01:10:07.661
You're better than me.

01:10:07.745 --> 01:10:11.248
I've always been better than you.
And your dad's not a stranger.

01:10:14.919 --> 01:10:15.753
What about me?

01:10:19.048 --> 01:10:20.382
Am I a stranger to you?

01:10:21.383 --> 01:10:24.178
-What?
-You've been distant lately towards me.

01:10:25.512 --> 01:10:26.555
Are you avoiding me?

01:10:29.475 --> 01:10:31.477
[sighs] It bothers me
when you act like this.

01:10:31.560 --> 01:10:34.605
You're distant and awkward.
It's not like old times.

01:10:36.065 --> 01:10:37.942
It can't be like old times forever.

01:10:39.652 --> 01:10:40.861
We're adults now.

01:10:41.737 --> 01:10:45.074
You have your life and I have mine.

01:10:46.200 --> 01:10:48.285
Let's stop staying stuck in the past.

01:10:49.036 --> 01:10:51.622
Stop doing childish things
like knocking on my window.

01:10:52.539 --> 01:10:54.416
Let's respect each other's privacy.

01:10:55.960 --> 01:10:57.294
[mellow music playing]

01:10:58.879 --> 01:10:59.713
I'll get going.

01:11:05.261 --> 01:11:06.470
[sighs deeply]

01:11:37.418 --> 01:11:38.419
[exhales]

01:11:52.182 --> 01:11:53.017
[exhales]

01:12:02.026 --> 01:12:04.695
[Seung-hyo] Stop doing childish things
like knocking on my window.

01:12:05.362 --> 01:12:07.156
Let's respect each other's privacy.

01:12:09.700 --> 01:12:10.534
[closes window]

01:12:30.637 --> 01:12:34.099
If I could crumple up feelings
like a mere letter,

01:12:35.309 --> 01:12:37.686
then could I have been
more comfortable around you?

01:12:44.693 --> 01:12:46.487
HYEREUNG COOKING SCHOOL

01:12:46.570 --> 01:12:49.073
Since cooking is my profession,

01:12:49.156 --> 01:12:53.494
people always ask me
how to make their food taste better.

01:12:53.577 --> 01:12:56.372
I always give them the same answer.

01:12:56.955 --> 01:12:59.291
If you think about the person
you're cooking for,

01:12:59.375 --> 01:13:02.169
it becomes more fun
and the food tastes better.

01:13:02.252 --> 01:13:06.799
The dish we'll make more fun
and taste better today is

01:13:07.549 --> 01:13:09.301
jijim nureumjeok.

01:13:09.385 --> 01:13:10.302
What?

01:13:10.386 --> 01:13:13.013
KOREAN FOOD CRAFTSMAN CLASS
JIJIM NUREUMJEOK

01:13:19.269 --> 01:13:20.896
[dogs barking in distance]

01:13:26.819 --> 01:13:28.112
[Seung-hyo] Jeez, you scared me.

01:13:28.946 --> 01:13:29.947
What?

01:13:31.198 --> 01:13:33.450
-What were you doing here?
-I was waiting for you. What?

01:13:34.576 --> 01:13:36.995
-Why?
-I mean, you helped my dad.

01:13:37.079 --> 01:13:39.540
And I wanted to repay
the favor for this and that.

01:13:40.457 --> 01:13:42.668
Here, take this.

01:13:43.210 --> 01:13:44.545
What is it?

01:13:44.628 --> 01:13:46.630
It's the first dish I made
in my cooking class.

01:13:49.633 --> 01:13:51.051
Why are you giving it to me?

01:13:57.850 --> 01:13:59.351
[Seok-ryu] You like these.

01:14:02.521 --> 01:14:05.441
Seung-hyo, how about some japchae?

01:14:05.524 --> 01:14:07.067
Do you want…

01:14:07.151 --> 01:14:09.027
Gosh, what do we do?

01:14:10.028 --> 01:14:12.948
He won't eat any Korean food.

01:14:13.031 --> 01:14:15.742
I made all the holiday dishes,
but he doesn't like any of them.

01:14:15.826 --> 01:14:18.912
So he ate eggs
and toast again today. Yeah.

01:14:18.996 --> 01:14:20.622
[Hye-suk] He's just not used to it.

01:14:20.706 --> 01:14:23.709
I should've done what I could
to make Korean food for him in France.

01:14:23.792 --> 01:14:25.502
[pleasant music playing]

01:14:26.962 --> 01:14:28.714
Eat this. It's good.

01:14:29.339 --> 01:14:30.674
No.

01:14:31.717 --> 01:14:34.595
Doesn't this look like a rainbow?

01:14:35.095 --> 01:14:36.472
[chimes]

01:14:37.681 --> 01:14:39.475
A rainbow?

01:14:39.558 --> 01:14:41.351
Yeah, a rainbow.

01:14:42.019 --> 01:14:43.103
A rainbow.

01:14:43.187 --> 01:14:44.730
[Mi-suk] He keeps saying "rainbow."

01:14:45.606 --> 01:14:47.649
Goodness! Hye-suk!

01:14:47.733 --> 01:14:50.652
Seung-hyo's eating!
The rainbow! He's eating it now!

01:14:50.736 --> 01:14:53.071
My gosh! He's eating now!

01:14:53.155 --> 01:14:55.782
You brat, you should've fed him
different foods!

01:14:58.160 --> 01:14:59.995
[Seok-ryu] Skewers
that look like rainbows.

01:15:02.372 --> 01:15:04.625
This was the first Korean dish
you ate here.

01:15:05.167 --> 01:15:06.752
Why did you remember that?

01:15:06.835 --> 01:15:08.962
I didn't remember it. I just…

01:15:09.922 --> 01:15:10.756
It came to mind.

01:15:10.839 --> 01:15:12.966
We've been friends for years.

01:15:13.717 --> 01:15:17.304
I bet I know more about you
than your parents do.

01:15:20.057 --> 01:15:21.225
You know me?

01:15:22.518 --> 01:15:23.519
You?

01:15:24.144 --> 01:15:25.896
-What?
-Seok-ryu…

01:15:27.814 --> 01:15:29.191
Your memories don't mean anything.

01:15:29.858 --> 01:15:31.443
They're all in the past.

01:15:31.944 --> 01:15:34.112
So stop bothering me
by reminding me of them.

01:15:34.196 --> 01:15:36.573
Why do you have to say it like that?

01:15:36.657 --> 01:15:38.075
Do you think I'm a pushover?

01:15:39.826 --> 01:15:42.287
I told you. We're not kids anymore.

01:15:43.247 --> 01:15:44.373
We're in our thirties now.

01:15:44.873 --> 01:15:47.417
We're not five anymore.
So why do you keep following me?

01:15:48.418 --> 01:15:51.547
-Why do you keep lingering around me?
-I didn't linger.

01:15:51.630 --> 01:15:52.798
I'm begging you.

01:15:54.424 --> 01:15:56.176
Just leave me alone.

01:15:57.010 --> 01:15:58.929
Stay out of my life from now on.

01:15:59.012 --> 01:16:00.097
No!

01:16:01.098 --> 01:16:02.975
I'm going to butt in all I want!

01:16:04.101 --> 01:16:07.104
Did you ask for my permission
before coming to my house back then?

01:16:07.187 --> 01:16:09.314
I'm going to keep
sticking my nose in your life.

01:16:09.856 --> 01:16:10.691
[exhales]

01:16:11.316 --> 01:16:13.986
[Seok-ryu] Because we're close.
I'm allowed to do that!

01:16:14.069 --> 01:16:16.113
Stop driving me crazy!

01:16:19.032 --> 01:16:20.367
Back then and now,

01:16:21.368 --> 01:16:22.786
you keep doing this…

01:16:25.956 --> 01:16:26.915
so I feel like…

01:16:29.167 --> 01:16:31.086
I'm going to lose my mind because of you!

01:16:33.213 --> 01:16:34.506
[mellow music playing]

01:16:37.426 --> 01:16:38.468
[exhales]

01:17:12.961 --> 01:17:15.714
[Seok-ryu] I know
all of Seung-hyo's firsts.

01:17:16.381 --> 01:17:17.382
[Mi-suk] Here.

01:17:18.050 --> 01:17:19.176
You go to a bathhouse.

01:17:19.259 --> 01:17:20.677
-Then, you drink this.
-Yeah!

01:17:22.596 --> 01:17:24.473
Seung-hyo, try it. It's good.

01:17:31.438 --> 01:17:32.356
[chuckles softly]

01:17:32.939 --> 01:17:34.941
[Seok-ryu] The first time
he had banana milk.

01:17:35.025 --> 01:17:36.234
[Mi-suk] Good, right?

01:17:37.611 --> 01:17:40.614
[young Seok-ryu] No!
I won't do it! I don't want to!

01:17:41.198 --> 01:17:43.116
[Seok-ryu] The first time
he started swimming.

01:17:43.200 --> 01:17:44.201
[crying]

01:17:47.704 --> 01:17:49.289
[Seok-ryu] What the hell?

01:17:52.000 --> 01:17:54.378
-Choisseung?
-Why are you staring at the ground?

01:17:54.461 --> 01:17:56.588
What's with you?
How are you suddenly taller than me?

01:17:57.214 --> 01:17:59.299
What have you been eating
in France during the break?

01:18:00.676 --> 01:18:02.803
The first time he became taller than me.

01:18:03.345 --> 01:18:04.763
How annoying.

01:18:08.517 --> 01:18:09.518
My turn?

01:18:10.310 --> 01:18:11.228
[Mo-eum groans softly]

01:18:12.354 --> 01:18:13.897
You're on a deserted island.

01:18:13.980 --> 01:18:15.649
What three things would you take?

01:18:15.732 --> 01:18:18.735
Fire-making tools, a water distiller,
and a Swiss Army knife.

01:18:18.819 --> 01:18:19.903
[Seung-hyo] Jeez.

01:18:19.986 --> 01:18:21.363
She answered so seriously.

01:18:21.947 --> 01:18:23.031
It's my turn now.

01:18:24.408 --> 01:18:25.617
[sighs]

01:18:25.701 --> 01:18:26.827
Choisseung?

01:18:27.619 --> 01:18:29.287
Do you have a crush on anyone right now?

01:18:38.130 --> 01:18:39.256
[Seok-ryu] He does.

01:18:39.339 --> 01:18:41.466
He does! He likes someone!

01:18:41.550 --> 01:18:42.509
He does.

01:18:42.968 --> 01:18:43.802
Who is it?

01:18:43.885 --> 01:18:46.596
Hey! Does she study architecture too?

01:18:46.680 --> 01:18:48.473
I think I know.
Does she go to your school?

01:18:48.557 --> 01:18:50.726
-[Mo-eum laughing]
-Is she in the same class?

01:18:50.809 --> 01:18:51.768
I don't know.

01:18:51.852 --> 01:18:54.563
[Seok-ryu] What do you mean?
Who else would know if you don't?

01:18:56.231 --> 01:18:57.858
The only thing I didn't know

01:18:58.442 --> 01:19:00.110
was who his first love was.

01:19:20.505 --> 01:19:21.506
[sighs deeply]

01:19:29.765 --> 01:19:30.766
Hey.

01:19:33.101 --> 01:19:34.644
Stop right there.

01:19:34.728 --> 01:19:35.729
Hey!

01:19:41.651 --> 01:19:43.236
[Seok-ryu breathing heavily]

01:19:57.667 --> 01:19:58.835
What you said earlier…

01:20:01.922 --> 01:20:03.632
what did you mean?

01:20:20.649 --> 01:20:22.359
YOUR FIRST

01:20:22.442 --> 01:20:28.532
YOUR FIRST LOVE

01:20:28.615 --> 01:20:29.950
[pop song playing]

01:21:01.356 --> 01:21:05.569
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:21:06.528 --> 01:21:08.613
[Seung-hyo] Why did you even show up here?

01:21:08.697 --> 01:21:10.156
And why now of all times?

01:21:11.366 --> 01:21:12.909
We have to kill that jerk.

01:21:12.993 --> 01:21:14.452
I want to kill him more.

01:21:14.536 --> 01:21:16.746
I'll kill this bastard and go to jail.

01:21:16.830 --> 01:21:17.956
Hey, you bastard!

01:21:18.039 --> 01:21:19.875
[Seok-ryu] You're eating
at a hotel for work.

01:21:19.958 --> 01:21:21.543
You're a great businessman.

01:21:21.626 --> 01:21:23.461
[Seung-hyo] Don't say her name anymore.

01:21:24.129 --> 01:21:25.797
Don't keep showing up either.

01:21:25.881 --> 01:21:28.341
It's already over between you two.

01:21:28.425 --> 01:21:31.720
[Mo-eum] Seung-hyo, you have to
save yourself from unrequited love.

01:21:31.803 --> 01:21:33.555
Even I can't rescue you.

01:21:34.097 --> 01:21:37.142
[Seung-hyo] I won't delay it any longer.
I'm going to say it this time.

01:21:40.687 --> 01:21:43.690
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
